{"jobs":[{"id":"2479c89e-8b13-415e-9fe5-5dfdc4be4f96","title":"Controller","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-04T22:36:30.919+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2479c89e-8b13-415e-9fe5-5dfdc4be4f96","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2479c89e-8b13-415e-9fe5-5dfdc4be4f96/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is seeking a highly motivated and proactive Controller to develop and execute accounting policies and procedures while scaling accounting systems and tools for growth. Reporting to the Chief Executive Officer, this individual will be responsible for directing the accounting activities of the company.  The ideal candidate is someone who enjoys the challenge of working at a fast-paced startup, solving problems, and pioneering processes to better streamline and enhance financial operations. This role requires someone who can both execute and lead. You’ll be responsible for running the accounting function day to day alongside your team, while also strengthening processes, building infrastructure, and guiding how the function grows within the company. You will be instrumental in coaching and mentoring your team while still being hands on.  You will play a critical role in ensuring that we build a premiere accounting function, while partnering across the business to ensure our systems and processes are running smoothly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own accounting, payroll, tax filing, invoicing, bank account tracking and reconciliation, expense management, budgeting, and payment processing via quickbooks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct and assist in the preparation and delivery of monthly, quarterly and year-end consolidated financial statements and notes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate any external audit of the consolidated financial statements and notes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish, implement and monitor accounting policies, practices and systems and internal control environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure taxes are filed on a timely basis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement effective processes to forecast, track and manage all cash receipts and disbursements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide comprehensive and timely reporting and analysis to management and other internal and external stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with external vendors regarding receivable collections</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure that all accounting, treasury and tax transactions and provisions are processed efficiently and recorded effectively in an accurate and timely manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay abreast of evolving legislation and ensure compliance with all tax law guidance regarding marketplaces, remote-first companies, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continually identify issues in both process and accounting for transactions and propose solutions (in conjunction with auditors)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience within accounting/finance at a growth-stage or late-stage startup, eCommerce or Marketplaces experience preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience at a Big 4 accounting firm required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical accounting knowledge plus working knowledge of tax</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to implement and maintain Internal Control over Financial Reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent oral, written, and quantitative communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert knowledge of US GAAP principles </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced proficiency with quickbooks (QBO experience preferred)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $175,000/year - $250,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives..</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is July 1st, 2026.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nAbout the position\n\n\n\nVetcove is seeking a highly motivated and proactive Controller to develop and execute accounting policies and procedures while scaling accounting systems and tools for growth. Reporting to the Chief Executive Officer, this individual will be responsible for directing the accounting activities of the company.  The ideal candidate is someone who enjoys the challenge of working at a fast-paced startup, solving problems, and pioneering processes to better streamline and enhance financial operations. This role requires someone who can both execute and lead. You’ll be responsible for running the accounting function day to day alongside your team, while also strengthening processes, building infrastructure, and guiding how the function grows within the company. You will be instrumental in coaching and mentoring your team while still being hands on.  You will play a critical role in ensuring that we build a premiere accounting function, while partnering across the business to ensure our systems and processes are running smoothly.\n\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\n - Own accounting, payroll, tax filing, invoicing, bank account tracking and reconciliation, expense management, budgeting, and payment processing via quickbooks\n\n - Direct and assist in the preparation and delivery of monthly, quarterly and year-end consolidated financial statements and notes\n\n - Coordinate any external audit of the consolidated financial statements and notes\n\n - Establish, implement and monitor accounting policies, practices and systems and internal control environment\n\n - Ensure taxes are filed on a timely basis\n\n - Implement effective processes to forecast, track and manage all cash receipts and disbursements\n\n - Provide comprehensive and timely reporting and analysis to management and other internal and external stakeholders\n\n - Communicate with external vendors regarding receivable collections\n\n - Ensure that all accounting, treasury and tax transactions and provisions are processed efficiently and recorded effectively in an accurate and timely manner\n\n - Stay abreast of evolving legislation and ensure compliance with all tax law guidance regarding marketplaces, remote-first companies, etc.\n\n - Continually identify issues in both process and accounting for transactions and propose solutions (in conjunction with auditors)\n\n\n\nYou should have\n\n - Experience within accounting/finance at a growth-stage or late-stage startup, eCommerce or Marketplaces experience preferred\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field required\n\n - Prior experience at a Big 4 accounting firm required.\n\n - Strong technical accounting knowledge plus working knowledge of tax\n\n - Proven ability to implement and maintain Internal Control over Financial Reporting\n\n - Excellent oral, written, and quantitative communication skills\n\n - Strong attention to detail\n\n - Expert knowledge of US GAAP principles \n\n - Advanced proficiency with quickbooks (QBO experience preferred)\n\n\n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $175,000/year - $250,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives..\n\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n\n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is July 1st, 2026.\n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2c68f84a-c437-41ad-b328-2fb3800febef","title":"Vet Clinic Support Associate","department":"Customer Experience ","team":"Customer Experience ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T20:18:38.455+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2c68f84a-c437-41ad-b328-2fb3800febef","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2c68f84a-c437-41ad-b328-2fb3800febef/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Support Associate is responsible for engaging with our vibrant community of veterinary professionals to support them in their critical purchasing decisions and processes through the use of the Vetcove platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Members of the support team work collaboratively to help provide our users an excellent experience on our platform through live chats, phone calls, emails, internal discussion boards, and platform demos This role plays a pivotal part in ensuring a positive and delightful day-to-day experience for every user leveraging the platform for their supply ordering needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of supporting and growing a large community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals through answering intercoms via our platform, troubleshooting, and working cross-functionally to help evolve our platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a relevant customer-facing role, as well as excellent written and verbal communication skills, are required. Knowledge of intercom and/or experience with other chat platforms is strongly preferred.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support existing Vetcove users by responding to user inquiries via live chat, email, and phone in a timely manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot issues quickly and explain scenarios/solutions in an easily digestible and effective manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle various daily and weekly admin responsibilities, such as proactive account management, item issue reports, item reviews, credit approvals, and more</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally to provide our engineering, partner, and corporate teams with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with vendor and industry partners to streamline communication and alerts between systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline support workflows</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1 year of relevant, customer facing work experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2 Year Associates Degree or 4 Year College Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in chat support preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Patience and compassion when handling difficult situations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to learn and help our customers succeed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality and excellent collaboration skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech/start-up work experience is a plus but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $50,000/year - $80,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $55,000 - $75,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nAbout the Position\n\nThe Support Associate is responsible for engaging with our vibrant community of veterinary professionals to support them in their critical purchasing decisions and processes through the use of the Vetcove platform.\n\n\n\nMembers of the support team work collaboratively to help provide our users an excellent experience on our platform through live chats, phone calls, emails, internal discussion boards, and platform demos This role plays a pivotal part in ensuring a positive and delightful day-to-day experience for every user leveraging the platform for their supply ordering needs.\n\n\n\nThe ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of supporting and growing a large community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals through answering intercoms via our platform, troubleshooting, and working cross-functionally to help evolve our platform.\n\n\n\nExperience in a relevant customer-facing role, as well as excellent written and verbal communication skills, are required. Knowledge of intercom and/or experience with other chat platforms is strongly preferred.\n\n\n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Support existing Vetcove users by responding to user inquiries via live chat, email, and phone in a timely manner\n\n - Troubleshoot issues quickly and explain scenarios/solutions in an easily digestible and effective manner\n\n - Handle various daily and weekly admin responsibilities, such as proactive account management, item issue reports, item reviews, credit approvals, and more\n\n - Work cross-functionally to provide our engineering, partner, and corporate teams with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools\n\n - Work with vendor and industry partners to streamline communication and alerts between systems\n\n - Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline support workflows\n   \n   \n\nYou should have\n\n - 1 year of relevant, customer facing work experience\n\n - 2 Year Associates Degree or 4 Year College Degree\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Experience in chat support preferred\n\n - Patience and compassion when handling difficult situations\n\n - Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities\n\n - A strong desire to learn and help our customers succeed\n\n - A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality and excellent collaboration skills\n\n - Tech/start-up work experience is a plus but not required\n\n\n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n\n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $50,000/year - $80,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $55,000 - $75,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.\n\n\n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ea8900cb-28f7-4c06-93dd-6391a4bfe936","title":"Vet Clinic Implementation Associate ","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T20:11:54.163+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/ea8900cb-28f7-4c06-93dd-6391a4bfe936","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/ea8900cb-28f7-4c06-93dd-6391a4bfe936/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Vet Clinic Implementation Associate at Vetcove is responsible for overseeing the end-to-end management of the large scale projects that enhance the customer experience for our users, and streamline processes. This role will be client facing as the point of contact for our external partners throughout the entire project lifecycle, while also being a liaison internally between our engineering and business teams. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate will be highly motivated and very skilled in the realm of multitasking, staying organized, and maintaining a sharp attention to detail. Success in this position requires a strong ability to effectively time manage, set expectations, and communicate clearly and effectively to multiple parties. In this position, one must manage multiple projects at a time, so ability to work in a fast-paced environment is a requirement. This role will require travel. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively communicate with the team and all stakeholders to set priorities, ensure that project milestones expectations are met, and determine team member expectations across departments as well as communicating directly with executives and leadership teams to provide progress updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop project plans and timeline to ensure that team members understand the expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify areas where team members are needed to ensure that project milestones and deliverables are completed according to the schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with leadership to define processes and milestones, and ensure we are on track to complete by our intended launch date</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide project updates on a consistent basis to various stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assign project tasks based on creative team members' individual strengths, skill sets, and experience levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding business goals and connecting them with prioritization of incoming project requests</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must have previous experience either working directly in a veterinary clinic OR working directly with clinics implementing new veterinary software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in managing different types of projects that involve developing partnership plans, preparing for integrations with 3rd parties, and strategizing for new feature and product launches </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organization and time management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building roadmaps, project plans and timelines with strong attention to details</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humility and willingness to roll up sleeves and take ownership of clearing any obstacles the team faces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working effectively in a heavily cross-functional, fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to hold others accountable for deliverables against tight timelines</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $60,000/year - $85,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $60,000 - $80,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nAbout the position\n\nThe Vet Clinic Implementation Associate at Vetcove is responsible for overseeing the end-to-end management of the large scale projects that enhance the customer experience for our users, and streamline processes. This role will be client facing as the point of contact for our external partners throughout the entire project lifecycle, while also being a liaison internally between our engineering and business teams. \n\nThe ideal candidate will be highly motivated and very skilled in the realm of multitasking, staying organized, and maintaining a sharp attention to detail. Success in this position requires a strong ability to effectively time manage, set expectations, and communicate clearly and effectively to multiple parties. In this position, one must manage multiple projects at a time, so ability to work in a fast-paced environment is a requirement. This role will require travel. \n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Effectively communicate with the team and all stakeholders to set priorities, ensure that project milestones expectations are met, and determine team member expectations across departments as well as communicating directly with executives and leadership teams to provide progress updates\n\n - Develop project plans and timeline to ensure that team members understand the expectations\n\n - Identify areas where team members are needed to ensure that project milestones and deliverables are completed according to the schedule\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with leadership to define processes and milestones, and ensure we are on track to complete by our intended launch date\n\n - Provide project updates on a consistent basis to various stakeholders\n\n - Assign project tasks based on creative team members' individual strengths, skill sets, and experience levels\n\n - Understanding business goals and connecting them with prioritization of incoming project requests\n\n \n\nYou should have\n\n - Must have previous experience either working directly in a veterinary clinic OR working directly with clinics implementing new veterinary software\n\n - Experience in managing different types of projects that involve developing partnership plans, preparing for integrations with 3rd parties, and strategizing for new feature and product launches \n\n - Excellent organization and time management\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills\n\n - Experience building roadmaps, project plans and timelines with strong attention to details\n\n - Humility and willingness to roll up sleeves and take ownership of clearing any obstacles the team faces\n\n - Experience working effectively in a heavily cross-functional, fast-paced environment\n\n - Ability to hold others accountable for deliverables against tight timelines\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $60,000/year - $85,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $60,000 - $80,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. \n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. \n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2be13241-43f5-4774-b421-f5e6e9e8fbec","title":"AI Integrations Staff Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:27:03.972+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2be13241-43f5-4774-b421-f5e6e9e8fbec","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/2be13241-43f5-4774-b421-f5e6e9e8fbec/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the position</strong></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is seeking an experienced Applied AI Staff Engineer to join our team. As an Applied AI Staff Engineer, you will be responsible for integrating cutting-edge AI models into our existing features to enhance our products' capabilities and deliver a better user experience. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving, highly collaborative team!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluating and selecting the most appropriate AI models for our products based on our business needs and requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build out evaluation frameworks and configure observability platforms for monitoring AI performance in production systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborating with our data science team to fine-tune AI models for optimal performance in our products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Developing and maintaining AI-powered application features using Python</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Testing and validating the performance of AI models in real-world scenarios and troubleshooting issues as they arise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Staying up-to-date with the latest advancements in AI technology and identifying opportunities for innovation within our products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with our CTO and engineering team, as well as across other functions to continuously evolve our platform and products</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>You should have</strong></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 4 years of experience in software development, including experience in building a professionally successful production application in a modern web framework</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of AI models, including familiarity with agent SDKs, agent harnesses, and fine-tuning AI models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong engineering fundamentals with various back-end technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to design new features around data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you are passionate about AI and have experience in integrating AI models into existing software systems, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity. Note that this role does <em>not</em> require designing and implementing new machine learning models, but rather integrating and fine-tuning existing models available in the market.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $150,000/year -$230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $160,000 - $210,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE POSITION\n\n \n\nVetcove is seeking an experienced Applied AI Staff Engineer to join our team. As an Applied AI Staff Engineer, you will be responsible for integrating cutting-edge AI models into our existing features to enhance our products' capabilities and deliver a better user experience. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving, highly collaborative team!\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n \n\n - Evaluating and selecting the most appropriate AI models for our products based on our business needs and requirements.\n\n - Design and build out evaluation frameworks and configure observability platforms for monitoring AI performance in production systems\n\n - Collaborating with our data science team to fine-tune AI models for optimal performance in our products.\n\n - Developing and maintaining AI-powered application features using Python\n\n - Testing and validating the performance of AI models in real-world scenarios and troubleshooting issues as they arise.\n\n - Staying up-to-date with the latest advancements in AI technology and identifying opportunities for innovation within our products.\n\n - Work directly with our CTO and engineering team, as well as across other functions to continuously evolve our platform and products\n\n \n\n\nYOU SHOULD HAVE\n\n \n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n\n - At least 4 years of experience in software development, including experience in building a professionally successful production application in a modern web framework\n\n - Strong knowledge of AI models, including familiarity with agent SDKs, agent harnesses, and fine-tuning AI models\n\n - Strong engineering fundamentals with various back-end technologies\n\n - Ability to design new features around data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind\n\n - A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality\n\n \n\nIf you are passionate about AI and have experience in integrating AI models into existing software systems, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity. Note that this role does not require designing and implementing new machine learning models, but rather integrating and fine-tuning existing models available in the market.\n\n \n \n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $150,000/year -$230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $160,000 - $210,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis. \n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"48a2f215-93be-4d01-be54-08222bc4c269","title":"Clinic Sales Manager","department":"Sales and Retention","team":"Sales and Retention","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:41:30.018+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/48a2f215-93be-4d01-be54-08222bc4c269","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/48a2f215-93be-4d01-be54-08222bc4c269/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Clinic Growth Manager you'll design and run the programs that keep thousands of veterinary clinics engaged, growing, and getting real value from Vetcove – and you'll know how to identify the ones who need a personal nudge and go get them.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll think in programs, not just conversations – using data, content, and community to move thousands of clinics at once.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and manage a clinic community program including newsletters, referral programs, peer spotlights, and online engagement initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and run clinic-focused seminars and educational webinars on topics like in-platform best practices, successful workflows, and platform updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop best practice playbooks, how-to guides, and self-serve resources that help clinics maximize platform value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead best practice sessions to share learnings, tips, and platform updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze usage trends, sales patterns, and platform engagement to identify underperforming clinics and build targeted re-engagement plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor key health metrics across the platform to flag at-risk accounts before churn becomes a risk</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a feedback loop between clinics and the product team: know what clinics need and advocate for it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools and partnership with the data team to build and maintain dashboards to track clinic health, engagement, and growth metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare regular business reviews with data-driven insights for internal stakeholders</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience in Community Engagement, Growth Marketing, Customer Success, Account Management, or a client-facing role, ideally in a SaaS or technology company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving measurable growth outcomes across a large customer base</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with data: You can pull a report, spot a trend, and translate it into action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to community programs, event coordination, or customer education initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A natural communicator who can hold a room in a seminar, build trust in a 1:1, and write a newsletter people actually read</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple programs and initiatives simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable shifting between program-level thinking and direct clinic conversations when the situation calls for it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at translating user feedback and behavioral data into program decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in veterinary, healthcare, or life sciences is a strong plus but not required</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Haves</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar CRM tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with customer health scoring or churn prediction frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a high-growth startup environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $140,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $130,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\nAs a Clinic Growth Manager you'll design and run the programs that keep thousands of veterinary clinics engaged, growing, and getting real value from Vetcove – and you'll know how to identify the ones who need a personal nudge and go get them.\n\n \n\nYou'll think in programs, not just conversations – using data, content, and community to move thousands of clinics at once.\n\n \n\nWhat You Will Do\n\n - Design and manage a clinic community program including newsletters, referral programs, peer spotlights, and online engagement initiatives\n\n - Develop and run clinic-focused seminars and educational webinars on topics like in-platform best practices, successful workflows, and platform updates\n\n - Develop best practice playbooks, how-to guides, and self-serve resources that help clinics maximize platform value\n\n - Lead best practice sessions to share learnings, tips, and platform updates\n\n - Analyze usage trends, sales patterns, and platform engagement to identify underperforming clinics and build targeted re-engagement plans\n\n - Monitor key health metrics across the platform to flag at-risk accounts before churn becomes a risk\n\n - Act as a feedback loop between clinics and the product team: know what clinics need and advocate for it\n\n - Leverage AI tools and partnership with the data team to build and maintain dashboards to track clinic health, engagement, and growth metrics\n\n - Prepare regular business reviews with data-driven insights for internal stakeholders\n\n \n\nWhat We’re Looking For\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 3–5 years of experience in Community Engagement, Growth Marketing, Customer Success, Account Management, or a client-facing role, ideally in a SaaS or technology company\n\n - A track record of driving measurable growth outcomes across a large customer base\n\n - Comfort with data: You can pull a report, spot a trend, and translate it into action\n\n - Experience building or contributing to community programs, event coordination, or customer education initiatives\n\n - A natural communicator who can hold a room in a seminar, build trust in a 1:1, and write a newsletter people actually read\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple programs and initiatives simultaneously\n\n - Comfortable shifting between program-level thinking and direct clinic conversations when the situation calls for it.\n\n - Skilled at translating user feedback and behavioral data into program decisions\n\n - Experience in veterinary, healthcare, or life sciences is a strong plus but not required\n\n \n\nNice to Haves\n\n - Familiarity with Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar CRM tools\n\n - Experience with customer health scoring or churn prediction frameworks\n\n - Prior experience in a high-growth startup environment\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $140,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $130,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"08e60ffb-e407-45f1-924a-8e28bde6b6c0","title":"Staff Design Engineer ","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-21T20:07:34.074+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/08e60ffb-e407-45f1-924a-8e28bde6b6c0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/08e60ffb-e407-45f1-924a-8e28bde6b6c0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Position</strong></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Staff Design Engineer at Vetcove, you’ll sit at the intersection of design and engineering. We believe the best user experiences, especially for our furry friends and the veterinarians that care for them, arise from engineers being intimately involved in the design process from the very first wireframe through pixel perfection. You’ll work closely with the design team to brainstorm and iterate on feature enhancements and new user experiences, ensuring a high quality implementation. You’ll be responsible for the highest level of polish across Vetcove’s desktop and mobile applications.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we are looking for:</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe there are a couple traits that will make you perfect for this role:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have an extraordinary attention to detail. Every pixel matters to you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You love React, and love building new React components. You have several years experience working with React and using the latest React features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a CSS guru. You love the challenge of building complex interactions purely through CSS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You truly love design and are passionate about exploring the latest design and interaction trends.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A passion for pets is always a big plus, but certainly not required!</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with product designers in designing new features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring Figma designs to life by implementing modular, reusable React components</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement interactions using highly flexible and performant CSS code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experiment with animations and micro-interactions that are best prototyped through code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with the front end engineering team to bridge front end logic with design</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have:</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 3 years of experience in software development, including experience in building a professionally successful production application using React.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A set of front end components and or designs you’ve implemented that you can share!</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $140,000/year - $220,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $145,000 - $195,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE POSITION\n\n \n\nAs a Staff Design Engineer at Vetcove, you’ll sit at the intersection of design and engineering. We believe the best user experiences, especially for our furry friends and the veterinarians that care for them, arise from engineers being intimately involved in the design process from the very first wireframe through pixel perfection. You’ll work closely with the design team to brainstorm and iterate on feature enhancements and new user experiences, ensuring a high quality implementation. You’ll be responsible for the highest level of polish across Vetcove’s desktop and mobile applications.\n\n \n\nWhat we are looking for:\n\n \n\nWe believe there are a couple traits that will make you perfect for this role:\n\n - You have an extraordinary attention to detail. Every pixel matters to you.\n\n - You love React, and love building new React components. You have several years experience working with React and using the latest React features.\n\n - You are a CSS guru. You love the challenge of building complex interactions purely through CSS.\n\n - You truly love design and are passionate about exploring the latest design and interaction trends.\n\n - A passion for pets is always a big plus, but certainly not required!\n\n \n\nWhat you’ll do:\n\n \n\n - Collaborate closely with product designers in designing new features\n\n - Bring Figma designs to life by implementing modular, reusable React components\n\n - Implement interactions using highly flexible and performant CSS code\n\n - Experiment with animations and micro-interactions that are best prototyped through code\n\n - Work closely with the front end engineering team to bridge front end logic with design\n\n \n\nYou should have:\n\n \n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n\n - At least 3 years of experience in software development, including experience in building a professionally successful production application using React.\n\n - A set of front end components and or designs you’ve implemented that you can share!\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n \n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $140,000/year - $220,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $145,000 - $195,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. \n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e2659573-d815-4572-99f1-5321e1ec9026","title":"Senior Engineering Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:04:53.103+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/e2659573-d815-4572-99f1-5321e1ec9026","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/e2659573-d815-4572-99f1-5321e1ec9026/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Senior Engineering Manager to lead a high impact team of software engineers with a strong focus on people leadership, mentorship, and engineer growth. We are looking for someone who enjoys coaching engineers, building strong teams, creating clarity, and helping people do the best work of their careers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Engineering Manager at Vetcove, you will help guide projects from conception to completion across much of the technology stack. Your involvement will span team leadership, execution planning, mentorship, hiring, career development, architecture discussions, technical strategy, and engineering process improvement. You should also be close to the code, able to understand technical tradeoffs, assist with code reviews, and help unblock engineers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a leader supporting the core features of the Vetcove platform, you will help ensure we are building intuitive, reliable, and innovative products that veterinary organizations depend on every day. You will work closely with engineers, product leaders, and company leadership to move quickly, maintain high technical standards, and support the long term growth of the team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About our team</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We believe every engineer at Vetcove should have a holistic view of the business and feel ownership across many areas of our technology stack. Our engineering leaders are no exception. We value managers who stay close to the code, understand the customer experience, and lead by creating clarity, developing people, and helping teams execute effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We move quickly in an industry that has historically been slow to adopt technology. As Vetcove continues expanding its offerings to better serve veterinary groups and supply chain partners, we are rapidly growing our engineering organization while maintaining a strong focus on code quality, system reliability, thoughtful product development, and strong people leadership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will have the opportunity to work closely with end users, support engineers across different stages of their careers, help the team tackle large scale infrastructure challenges, and shape how our engineering organization evolves. We operate in a fully remote environment that emphasizes ownership, autonomy, communication, and teamwork.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and grow a team of engineers with a strong focus on people development, team health, and career growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support engineers through regular coaching, feedback, goal setting, and career development conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create clarity for the team around priorities, expectations, ownership, and successful outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product and engineering leadership to define priorities, drive execution, and deliver successful outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support projects from early planning and architecture through implementation, rollout, and long term maintenance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay close to the technical work by understanding system design, reviewing technical plans, participating in architecture discussions, and helping evaluate tradeoffs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with code reviews and technical feedback where helpful, while primarily enabling the team rather than acting as a regular direct contributor</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help unblock engineers by providing context, asking the right questions, connecting people, and clarifying priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the conceptualization and technical design of new ideas and product enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help drive architectural improvements that prioritize scalability, reliability, maintainability, and performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reinforce strong engineering standards, development practices, testing habits, and ownership across the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help promote a culture of quality, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with our CTO, engineering leadership, and cross functional partners to continuously evolve our products and technical foundation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support hiring, onboarding, mentorship, performance feedback, and career development across the engineering organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a collaborative, low ego, high ownership culture in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you should have</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of professional software engineering experience, preferably building modern web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing, leading, or mentoring engineers in a fast moving technical environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine interest in people management, coaching, feedback, and engineer growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical judgment and the ability to understand code, architecture, system design, and engineering tradeoffs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort assisting with code reviews and technical discussions, even if you are not expected to contribute production code regularly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree required, ideally in Computer Science</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to design systems and features with scalability, security, reliability, and performance in mind</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with databases and analyzing queries for optimization opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year -$230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000 - $215,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nAbout the Position\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Senior Engineering Manager to lead a high impact team of software engineers with a strong focus on people leadership, mentorship, and engineer growth. We are looking for someone who enjoys coaching engineers, building strong teams, creating clarity, and helping people do the best work of their careers.\n\nAs a Senior Engineering Manager at Vetcove, you will help guide projects from conception to completion across much of the technology stack. Your involvement will span team leadership, execution planning, mentorship, hiring, career development, architecture discussions, technical strategy, and engineering process improvement. You should also be close to the code, able to understand technical tradeoffs, assist with code reviews, and help unblock engineers.\n\nAs a leader supporting the core features of the Vetcove platform, you will help ensure we are building intuitive, reliable, and innovative products that veterinary organizations depend on every day. You will work closely with engineers, product leaders, and company leadership to move quickly, maintain high technical standards, and support the long term growth of the team.\n\n \n\nAbout our team\n\n\nWe believe every engineer at Vetcove should have a holistic view of the business and feel ownership across many areas of our technology stack. Our engineering leaders are no exception. We value managers who stay close to the code, understand the customer experience, and lead by creating clarity, developing people, and helping teams execute effectively.\n\nWe move quickly in an industry that has historically been slow to adopt technology. As Vetcove continues expanding its offerings to better serve veterinary groups and supply chain partners, we are rapidly growing our engineering organization while maintaining a strong focus on code quality, system reliability, thoughtful product development, and strong people leadership.\n\nYou will have the opportunity to work closely with end users, support engineers across different stages of their careers, help the team tackle large scale infrastructure challenges, and shape how our engineering organization evolves. We operate in a fully remote environment that emphasizes ownership, autonomy, communication, and teamwork.\n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n \n\n - Lead, mentor, and grow a team of engineers with a strong focus on people development, team health, and career growth\n\n - Support engineers through regular coaching, feedback, goal setting, and career development conversations\n\n - Create clarity for the team around priorities, expectations, ownership, and successful outcomes\n\n - Partner closely with product and engineering leadership to define priorities, drive execution, and deliver successful outcomes\n\n - Support projects from early planning and architecture through implementation, rollout, and long term maintenance\n\n - Stay close to the technical work by understanding system design, reviewing technical plans, participating in architecture discussions, and helping evaluate tradeoffs\n\n - Assist with code reviews and technical feedback where helpful, while primarily enabling the team rather than acting as a regular direct contributor\n\n - Help unblock engineers by providing context, asking the right questions, connecting people, and clarifying priorities\n\n - Contribute to the conceptualization and technical design of new ideas and product enhancements\n\n - Help drive architectural improvements that prioritize scalability, reliability, maintainability, and performance\n\n - Reinforce strong engineering standards, development practices, testing habits, and ownership across the team\n\n - Help promote a culture of quality, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement\n\n - Work directly with our CTO, engineering leadership, and cross functional partners to continuously evolve our products and technical foundation\n\n - Support hiring, onboarding, mentorship, performance feedback, and career development across the engineering organization\n\n - Foster a collaborative, low ego, high ownership culture in a fully remote environment\n\n \n\nWhat you should have\n\n \n\n - 7+ years of professional software engineering experience, preferably building modern web applications\n\n - Experience managing, leading, or mentoring engineers in a fast moving technical environment\n\n - A genuine interest in people management, coaching, feedback, and engineer growth\n\n - Strong technical judgment and the ability to understand code, architecture, system design, and engineering tradeoffs\n\n - Comfort assisting with code reviews and technical discussions, even if you are not expected to contribute production code regularly\n\n - Bachelor's Degree required, ideally in Computer Science\n\n - Ability to design systems and features with scalability, security, reliability, and performance in mind\n\n - Experience working with databases and analyzing queries for optimization opportunities\n\n - Comfortable working in a fully remote environment\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year -$230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000 - $215,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7f077e0c-37aa-477f-b748-c29eed12dcf9","title":"Associate Account Manager","department":"Account Management ","team":"Account Management ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:28:45.220+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/7f077e0c-37aa-477f-b748-c29eed12dcf9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/7f077e0c-37aa-477f-b748-c29eed12dcf9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Associate Account Manager Role for Vetcove’s Brand Partnerships team provides support to help maintain relationships with our largest partners. This is accomplished through providing marketing campaign expertise and skillful project management in order to deliver above and beyond customer service. This is an outstanding opportunity to build and manage key client relationships, be a platform and product expert, and act as our partners’ go-to for all aspects related to the campaign lifecycle. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will report to a Senior Account Manager and primarily focus on supporting the Senior Account Manager in covering Vetcove’s biggest partners. The Associate Account Manager will also have the opportunity to work toward independent coverage of SMB accounts. Exceptional candidates in this role will be mentored by their managers with the goal of covering larger accounts in the future. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is responsible for partnering with our Data Scientists and other Account Managers. to foster client relationships, educate advertisers, implement thoughtful marketing campaign strategies, and manage the formulation and delivery of key performance insights and recommendations to support campaign objectives. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is an analytical and detail-oriented individual with the capacity and desire to succeed in a high growth environment. They have a strong ability to successfully collaborate with others, and thrive in a client facing role. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success in this position requires strong project management skills with a focus on client service, and the ability to thrive in a dynamic, team-focused environment delivering against partner goals and objectives. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the main point of contact for all client day-to-day communication and oversight</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Senior Partner Account Manager on recurring client tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project manage campaign execution to ensure all campaign requirements and timelines are met </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generate and analyze detailed campaign reporting; provide detailed insights and analysis for clients and suggest optimization strategies for increased performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work collaboratively with data scientists and other account managers to craft narratives and prove customer value through comprehensive business reviews and strategic touch-points, both over the phone and through on-site meetings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Educate and guide new and existing clients on best practices, on-board new clients and proactively address areas where improvement is needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nurture relationships to be sure they understand Vetcove’s value and how we can fit into long term strategy</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You Should Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ Years in account management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent time and process management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in developing client facing reports with actionable insights and recommendations </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in developing and presenting data analyses and partner business reviews </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced in compiling, documenting and communicating client requirements to internal stakeholders (e.g., Finance, C-Suite, Engineering)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of entire Microsoft Office suite, with an emphasis on PowerPoint and Excel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in Tableau or other database visualization tools La plus but not required </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in client relationship building and willingness to travel for client-facing events </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment</p></li></ul><h3></h3><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $60,000/year - $85,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $60,000 - $75,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the position\n\nThe Associate Account Manager Role for Vetcove’s Brand Partnerships team provides support to help maintain relationships with our largest partners. This is accomplished through providing marketing campaign expertise and skillful project management in order to deliver above and beyond customer service. This is an outstanding opportunity to build and manage key client relationships, be a platform and product expert, and act as our partners’ go-to for all aspects related to the campaign lifecycle. \n\n \n\nThis role will report to a Senior Account Manager and primarily focus on supporting the Senior Account Manager in covering Vetcove’s biggest partners. The Associate Account Manager will also have the opportunity to work toward independent coverage of SMB accounts. Exceptional candidates in this role will be mentored by their managers with the goal of covering larger accounts in the future. \n\n \n\nThis role is responsible for partnering with our Data Scientists and other Account Managers. to foster client relationships, educate advertisers, implement thoughtful marketing campaign strategies, and manage the formulation and delivery of key performance insights and recommendations to support campaign objectives. \n\n \n\nThe ideal candidate is an analytical and detail-oriented individual with the capacity and desire to succeed in a high growth environment. They have a strong ability to successfully collaborate with others, and thrive in a client facing role. \n\n \n\nSuccess in this position requires strong project management skills with a focus on client service, and the ability to thrive in a dynamic, team-focused environment delivering against partner goals and objectives. \n\n \n\nWhat You'll do\n\n - Act as the main point of contact for all client day-to-day communication and oversight\n\n - Collaborate with the Senior Partner Account Manager on recurring client tasks\n\n - Project manage campaign execution to ensure all campaign requirements and timelines are met \n\n - Generate and analyze detailed campaign reporting; provide detailed insights and analysis for clients and suggest optimization strategies for increased performance\n\n - Work collaboratively with data scientists and other account managers to craft narratives and prove customer value through comprehensive business reviews and strategic touch-points, both over the phone and through on-site meetings\n\n - Educate and guide new and existing clients on best practices, on-board new clients and proactively address areas where improvement is needed\n\n - Nurture relationships to be sure they understand Vetcove’s value and how we can fit into long term strategy\n\n \n\nYou Should Have\n\n - 1+ Years in account management\n\n - Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills\n\n - Excellent time and process management skills\n\n - Strong analytical skills \n\n - Experience in developing client facing reports with actionable insights and recommendations \n\n - Experience in developing and presenting data analyses and partner business reviews \n\n - Experienced in compiling, documenting and communicating client requirements to internal stakeholders (e.g., Finance, C-Suite, Engineering)\n\n - Strong working knowledge of entire Microsoft Office suite, with an emphasis on PowerPoint and Excel\n\n - Experience in Tableau or other database visualization tools La plus but not required \n\n - Interest in client relationship building and willingness to travel for client-facing events \n\n - A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment\n\n\n\n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $60,000/year - $85,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $60,000 - $75,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"98e6e3cd-47d8-4f0c-ae93-5153888ec98d","title":"Senior Product Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T17:49:03.679+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/98e6e3cd-47d8-4f0c-ae93-5153888ec98d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/98e6e3cd-47d8-4f0c-ae93-5153888ec98d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Product Manager at Vetcove, you’ll be at the heart of enhancing and scaling the platforms that power veterinary clinics and their pet parents. You will own high-impact product initiatives end-to-end, from defining strategy and roadmap to execution and post-launch optimization. You will drive cross-functional alignment, lead complex initiatives, and proactively identify opportunities to improve user experience, operational efficiency, and long-term platform scalability. You will monitor product performance and feedback, oversee robust quality assurance processes, and remove roadblocks that impact customer growth and retention. You will work closely with internal team members including account managers, onboarding associates, engineering, data, design, and support. You will also build strong relationships with external stakeholders, including veterinary clinics and pet parents. You will play a critical role in defining product vision, evaluating tradeoffs, and assessing strengths, opportunities, and risks associated with software products and services.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn’t just another product role—it’s an opportunity to shape the long-term strategy of a platform trusted by thousands of veterinary professionals. If you're passionate about solving meaningful challenges at scale, leading cross-functional teams, and delivering measurable business impact, we’d love to have you on board.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Our Team</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in an industry rapidly embracing technology. Our platform powers the day-to-day operations of veterinary clinics, from medical records to online shopping, but our mission goes beyond software—we’re creating a better, more efficient way for clinics to serve their patients</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Manager, you’ll work closely with engineers, onboarding specialists, and support teams to bridge the gap between product and users. Your insights will drive improvements, ensuring our platform evolves to meet the ever-changing needs of veterinary clinics and pet parents</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Product Strategy &amp; Roadmap</strong>: Define and own product strategy for key areas of the platform, translating company goals and customer insights into a clear, prioritized roadmap.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead Complex Initiatives: </strong>Oversee large, cross-functional projects from discovery through launch and iteration, ensuring on-time delivery and measurable impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn Feedback &amp; Data into Action: </strong>Synthesize qualitative feedback and quantitative data to identify opportunities, validate hypotheses, and inform strategic decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Optimize Product Performance:</strong> Establish and monitor KPIs, analyze product performance trends, and lead initiatives to improve adoption, engagement, retention, and revenue outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strengthen Cross-Functional Alignment:</strong> Partner with engineering, design, data, onboarding, and support to align on requirements, scope, tradeoffs, and success metrics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Elevate Product Documentation &amp; Processes: </strong>Create detailed product requirement documents, user stories, and technical specifications to ensure clarity and execution excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ensure High-Quality Delivery: </strong>Lead comprehensive QA processes, define acceptance criteria, and uphold a high bar for user experience and product reliability.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mentor &amp; Influence: </strong>Provide guidance to junior product managers and influence stakeholders across departments to foster strong product thinking throughout the organization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Go-to-Market &amp; Enablement:</strong> Partner with internal teams to ensure successful launches, create training materials, and support feature adoption across customers and internal stakeholders.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> A four-year college degree and 5+ years of progressive product management experience, including ownership of complex product areas and demonstrated success delivering strategic, cross-functional initiatives that drive measurable business impact in a SaaS or technology-driven environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Skills:</strong> Proven ability to define and execute product strategy, manage multi-quarter roadmaps, lead discovery and experimentation efforts, and partner closely with engineering and design to ship scalable, high-quality solutions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic Thinker:</strong> Strong track record of setting long-term product vision, balancing short-term wins with long-term platform investments, and making principled tradeoffs aligned with company objectives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data-Driven Decision Maker:</strong> Advanced analytical capabilities with experience defining KPIs, building business cases, leveraging experimentation frameworks, and using data analytics tools to inform prioritization and measure success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Execution Excellence:</strong> Extensive experience writing detailed product requirement documents, leading sprint planning and backlog grooming, managing stakeholder expectations, and delivering complex launches with operational rigor.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Communicator &amp; Influencer:</strong> Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with experience influencing senior stakeholders and driving alignment across diverse, cross-functional teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer-Obsessed:</strong> Deep commitment to understanding user workflows, conducting research and interviews, and translating insights into impactful product improvements.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational Leadership:</strong> Demonstrated ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, mentor junior team members, and lead without direct authority.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tech-Savvy:</strong> Strong understanding of technical architecture, APIs, integrations, and system design considerations; comfort engaging in technical discussions and evaluating implementation tradeoffs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $120,000/year - $210,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $150,000 - $190,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\n \n\nAs a Senior Product Manager at Vetcove, you’ll be at the heart of enhancing and scaling the platforms that power veterinary clinics and their pet parents. You will own high-impact product initiatives end-to-end, from defining strategy and roadmap to execution and post-launch optimization. You will drive cross-functional alignment, lead complex initiatives, and proactively identify opportunities to improve user experience, operational efficiency, and long-term platform scalability. You will monitor product performance and feedback, oversee robust quality assurance processes, and remove roadblocks that impact customer growth and retention. You will work closely with internal team members including account managers, onboarding associates, engineering, data, design, and support. You will also build strong relationships with external stakeholders, including veterinary clinics and pet parents. You will play a critical role in defining product vision, evaluating tradeoffs, and assessing strengths, opportunities, and risks associated with software products and services.\n\nThis isn’t just another product role—it’s an opportunity to shape the long-term strategy of a platform trusted by thousands of veterinary professionals. If you're passionate about solving meaningful challenges at scale, leading cross-functional teams, and delivering measurable business impact, we’d love to have you on board.\n\n \n\nAbout Our Team\n\n \n\nWe’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in an industry rapidly embracing technology. Our platform powers the day-to-day operations of veterinary clinics, from medical records to online shopping, but our mission goes beyond software—we’re creating a better, more efficient way for clinics to serve their patients\n\n \n\nAs a Product Manager, you’ll work closely with engineers, onboarding specialists, and support teams to bridge the gap between product and users. Your insights will drive improvements, ensuring our platform evolves to meet the ever-changing needs of veterinary clinics and pet parents\n\n \n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nDrive Product Strategy & Roadmap: Define and own product strategy for key areas of the platform, translating company goals and customer insights into a clear, prioritized roadmap.\n\nLead Complex Initiatives: Oversee large, cross-functional projects from discovery through launch and iteration, ensuring on-time delivery and measurable impact.\n\nTurn Feedback & Data into Action: Synthesize qualitative feedback and quantitative data to identify opportunities, validate hypotheses, and inform strategic decisions.\n\nOptimize Product Performance: Establish and monitor KPIs, analyze product performance trends, and lead initiatives to improve adoption, engagement, retention, and revenue outcomes.\n\nStrengthen Cross-Functional Alignment: Partner with engineering, design, data, onboarding, and support to align on requirements, scope, tradeoffs, and success metrics.\n\nElevate Product Documentation & Processes: Create detailed product requirement documents, user stories, and technical specifications to ensure clarity and execution excellence.\n\nEnsure High-Quality Delivery: Lead comprehensive QA processes, define acceptance criteria, and uphold a high bar for user experience and product reliability.\n\nMentor & Influence: Provide guidance to junior product managers and influence stakeholders across departments to foster strong product thinking throughout the organization.\n\nDrive Go-to-Market & Enablement: Partner with internal teams to ensure successful launches, create training materials, and support feature adoption across customers and internal stakeholders.\n\n \n\nWhat We’re Looking For\n\nExperience: A four-year college degree and 5+ years of progressive product management experience, including ownership of complex product areas and demonstrated success delivering strategic, cross-functional initiatives that drive measurable business impact in a SaaS or technology-driven environment.\n\nSkills: Proven ability to define and execute product strategy, manage multi-quarter roadmaps, lead discovery and experimentation efforts, and partner closely with engineering and design to ship scalable, high-quality solutions.\n\nStrategic Thinker: Strong track record of setting long-term product vision, balancing short-term wins with long-term platform investments, and making principled tradeoffs aligned with company objectives.\n\nData-Driven Decision Maker: Advanced analytical capabilities with experience defining KPIs, building business cases, leveraging experimentation frameworks, and using data analytics tools to inform prioritization and measure success.\n\nExecution Excellence: Extensive experience writing detailed product requirement documents, leading sprint planning and backlog grooming, managing stakeholder expectations, and delivering complex launches with operational rigor.\n\nStrong Communicator & Influencer: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with experience influencing senior stakeholders and driving alignment across diverse, cross-functional teams.\n\nCustomer-Obsessed: Deep commitment to understanding user workflows, conducting research and interviews, and translating insights into impactful product improvements.\n\nOrganizational Leadership: Demonstrated ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, mentor junior team members, and lead without direct authority.\n\nTech-Savvy: Strong understanding of technical architecture, APIs, integrations, and system design considerations; comfort engaging in technical discussions and evaluating implementation tradeoffs.\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $120,000/year - $210,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $150,000 - $190,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n \n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"50aa9825-e364-4a44-8c6e-655690404da0","title":"Customer Support Manager","department":"Customer Experience ","team":"Customer Experience ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:55:03.892+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/50aa9825-e364-4a44-8c6e-655690404da0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/50aa9825-e364-4a44-8c6e-655690404da0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a Customer Support Manager to support the CX organization and our customers through the development and optimization of processes that ensure the best customer support and strategy as we scale. You will be leading a team of support associates in onboarding, training, measuring objectives, and enhancing processes. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Members of the CX team work collaboratively to help provide our users an excellent experience on our platform through live chats, phone calls, emails, internal discussion boards, educational courses, community events, collaborative content, and more. This role plays a pivotal part in ensuring the team's success in providing both an incredible first impression during the onboarding process, and a delightful day-to-day experience for every user and partner moving forward. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of supporting and growing a large community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals through answering intercoms via our platform, troubleshooting, and working cross-functionally to help evolve our platform.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the “Voice of CX\", raising key needs during planning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Leadership to understand the business processes, pain points, and goals of the organization </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage a team of support associates, provide training, onboarding, and measure performance </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interview and help scale the support team </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and promote company best practices and standards for support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally to provide our engineering, partner, and corporate teams with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with vendor and industry partners to streamline communication and alerts between systems </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline CX workflows</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in customer experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of management experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of intercom or similar ticketing systems </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have worked within multichannel support operations (chat, email, phone) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Patience and compassion when handling difficult situations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to learn and help our customers succeed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality and excellent collaboration skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech/start-up work experience is a plus but not required</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $85,000/year - $130,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $110,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\nWe are seeking a Customer Support Manager to support the CX organization and our customers through the development and optimization of processes that ensure the best customer support and strategy as we scale. You will be leading a team of support associates in onboarding, training, measuring objectives, and enhancing processes. \n\n \n\nMembers of the CX team work collaboratively to help provide our users an excellent experience on our platform through live chats, phone calls, emails, internal discussion boards, educational courses, community events, collaborative content, and more. This role plays a pivotal part in ensuring the team's success in providing both an incredible first impression during the onboarding process, and a delightful day-to-day experience for every user and partner moving forward. \n\n \n\nThe ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced, team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of supporting and growing a large community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals through answering intercoms via our platform, troubleshooting, and working cross-functionally to help evolve our platform.\n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Act as the “Voice of CX\", raising key needs during planning\n\n - Partner with Leadership to understand the business processes, pain points, and goals of the organization \n\n - Manage a team of support associates, provide training, onboarding, and measure performance \n\n - Interview and help scale the support team \n\n - Maintain and promote company best practices and standards for support\n\n - Work cross-functionally to provide our engineering, partner, and corporate teams with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools \n\n - Work with vendor and industry partners to streamline communication and alerts between systems \n\n - Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline CX workflows\n\n \n\nYou should have\n\n - 3+ years of experience in customer experience \n\n - 1+ years of management experience \n\n - Knowledge of intercom or similar ticketing systems \n\n - You have worked within multichannel support operations (chat, email, phone) \n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Patience and compassion when handling difficult situations\n\n - Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities\n\n - A strong desire to learn and help our customers succeed\n\n - A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality and excellent collaboration skills\n\n - Tech/start-up work experience is a plus but not required\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $85,000/year - $130,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $110,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"baa31952-a27a-4f88-8b4c-d5cf21959aa7","title":"Product Operations Associate","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:01:06.117+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/baa31952-a27a-4f88-8b4c-d5cf21959aa7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/baa31952-a27a-4f88-8b4c-d5cf21959aa7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Product Operations Associate at Vetcove, you'll play a critical role in keeping our product teams running smoothly and efficiently. You'll sit at the intersection of product, engineering, design, and customer-facing teams — helping translate user feedback into actionable insights, supporting product launches, and ensuring our processes scale as we grow. This is an ideal role for someone who is eager to develop deep operational expertise and grow within a fast-moving, mission-driven company.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Support Product Launches:</em> Partner with product managers, onboarding, and support teams to coordinate go-to-market activities, create training materials, and track feature adoption post-launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Work with Integration Partners:</em> Coordinate and lead discussions between integration partners and engineering teams and overseeing new integrations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Synthesize User Feedback:</em> Collect and organize qualitative feedback from clinics, pet parents, and internal stakeholders, and surface patterns and themes to inform product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Maintain Product Documentation:</em> Draft and maintain product requirement documents, user stories, release notes, and internal process guides to ensure clarity across teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Track &amp; Report on KPIs:</em> Monitor product performance dashboards, flag anomalies, and compile regular reports to help product managers stay on top of key metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Coordinate Cross-Functional Workflows:</em> Help manage sprint planning logistics, backlog grooming, and cross-team communication to keep initiatives on track.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Support QA Processes:</em> Assist with quality assurance testing, document bugs and edge cases, and help define acceptance criteria alongside product and engineering teams.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in product operations, business operations, project coordination, or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills with exceptional attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working with data, including experience with spreadsheets, dashboards, or basic analytics tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to juggle multiple workstreams and deadlines in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity about technology and a desire to understand how software products are built and used</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: exposure to SaaS products, healthcare or veterinary tech, or customer-facing roles</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $70,000/year -$110,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $75,000 - $105,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Role\n\n \n\nAs a Product Operations Associate at Vetcove, you'll play a critical role in keeping our product teams running smoothly and efficiently. You'll sit at the intersection of product, engineering, design, and customer-facing teams — helping translate user feedback into actionable insights, supporting product launches, and ensuring our processes scale as we grow. This is an ideal role for someone who is eager to develop deep operational expertise and grow within a fast-moving, mission-driven company.\n\n \n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n \n\n - Support Product Launches: Partner with product managers, onboarding, and support teams to coordinate go-to-market activities, create training materials, and track feature adoption post-launch.\n\n - Work with Integration Partners: Coordinate and lead discussions between integration partners and engineering teams and overseeing new integrations.\n\n - Synthesize User Feedback: Collect and organize qualitative feedback from clinics, pet parents, and internal stakeholders, and surface patterns and themes to inform product decisions.\n\n - Maintain Product Documentation: Draft and maintain product requirement documents, user stories, release notes, and internal process guides to ensure clarity across teams.\n\n - Track & Report on KPIs: Monitor product performance dashboards, flag anomalies, and compile regular reports to help product managers stay on top of key metrics.\n\n - Coordinate Cross-Functional Workflows: Help manage sprint planning logistics, backlog grooming, and cross-team communication to keep initiatives on track.\n\n - Support QA Processes: Assist with quality assurance testing, document bugs and edge cases, and help define acceptance criteria alongside product and engineering teams.\n\n \n\nWhat We're Looking For\n\n \n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 3+ years of experience in product operations, business operations, project coordination, or a related role\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills with exceptional attention to detail\n\n - Comfort working with data, including experience with spreadsheets, dashboards, or basic analytics tools\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to juggle multiple workstreams and deadlines in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Curiosity about technology and a desire to understand how software products are built and used\n\n - Bonus: exposure to SaaS products, healthcare or veterinary tech, or customer-facing roles\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $70,000/year -$110,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $75,000 - $105,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ff2f4c31-bbca-4f3c-8bf0-477d87cd41ae","title":"Associate General Counsel ","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:29:53.811+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/ff2f4c31-bbca-4f3c-8bf0-477d87cd41ae","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/ff2f4c31-bbca-4f3c-8bf0-477d87cd41ae/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Associate General Counsel will be a key member of Vetcove’s legal team and a trusted partner to teams across the business. This role is ideal for an attorney who thrives in a high-growth startup environment, brings a strong work ethic and ownership mindset to every project, enjoys tackling problems big and small, and wants to help build the legal infrastructure for a rapidly expanding technology company operating in highly regulated markets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Vetcove’s legal team, business leadership, product, and operations teams on a wide range of legal matters, including commercial contracting, product counseling, regulatory analysis, privacy, data security, intellectual property, and strategic growth initiatives. You should be excited to jump into new areas, master unfamiliar legal frameworks, and help the business move quickly while thoughtfully managing risk.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About our Team</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove’s legal team is deeply embedded in the business and works cross-functionally across nearly every major company initiative. We support a suite of products serving veterinary hospitals, corporate veterinary groups, manufacturers, distributors, animal health suppliers, and pet parents, which means our legal work touches SaaS, ecommerce, marketplace operations, pharmacy, veterinary practice regulations, FDA, DEA, privacy, telecommunications, consumer protection, and emerging technology.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We move quickly and expect our lawyers to be practical, proactive, and business-minded. You will not be limited to a narrow legal lane. Instead, you will be expected to understand the company’s products, customers, commercial goals, and regulatory environment, and to help craft thoughtful, scalable solutions. This is a role for someone who wants to become a true partner to business leadership and help shape the legal strategy of a company building the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, negotiate, and manage a wide range of commercial agreements, including SaaS agreements, MSAs, SOWs, order forms, NDAs, DPAs, vendor agreements, distribution agreements, partnership agreements, and other strategic commercial contracts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with business leadership, product, operations, and finance to support enterprise deals and strategic initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise on product development and product launches, including identifying legal risks and developing practical, business-oriented solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop expertise in new and evolving legal areas relevant to Vetcove’s business, including telecommunications, consumer protection, privacy, FDA, DEA, veterinary practice laws, pharmacy laws, ecommerce, marketplace regulation, and related compliance frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help translate complex legal and regulatory requirements into practical guidance for product, engineering, operations, and business teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support strategic growth initiatives, including new products, new markets, new commercial models, and new regulated workflows</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years of legal experience, including experience at a top-tier law firm</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">J.D. from an accredited law school and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial contracting experience, particularly with SaaS, technology, enterprise customers, MSAs, SOWs, order forms, DPAs, vendor agreements, and related commercial agreements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent drafting, negotiation, and issue-spotting skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Very strong work ethic and desire to dive deeply into the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience advising high-growth technology companies, SaaS businesses, regulated businesses, or enterprise software companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and enthusiasm for learning new and evolving regulatory frameworks, and translating them into practical guidance for the business team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, ownership-oriented mindset and a strong desire to solve problems rather than simply identify them</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $180,000/year - $230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There may be a different range applicable to specific work locations.</strong> For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000-$230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects base annual compensation and does not include bonus, equity, or other incentives.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits package. Please refer to the “Benefits” section above for more details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\nThe Associate General Counsel will be a key member of Vetcove’s legal team and a trusted partner to teams across the business. This role is ideal for an attorney who thrives in a high-growth startup environment, brings a strong work ethic and ownership mindset to every project, enjoys tackling problems big and small, and wants to help build the legal infrastructure for a rapidly expanding technology company operating in highly regulated markets.\n\n \n\nYou will work closely with Vetcove’s legal team, business leadership, product, and operations teams on a wide range of legal matters, including commercial contracting, product counseling, regulatory analysis, privacy, data security, intellectual property, and strategic growth initiatives. You should be excited to jump into new areas, master unfamiliar legal frameworks, and help the business move quickly while thoughtfully managing risk.\n\n \n\nAbout our Team\n\nVetcove’s legal team is deeply embedded in the business and works cross-functionally across nearly every major company initiative. We support a suite of products serving veterinary hospitals, corporate veterinary groups, manufacturers, distributors, animal health suppliers, and pet parents, which means our legal work touches SaaS, ecommerce, marketplace operations, pharmacy, veterinary practice regulations, FDA, DEA, privacy, telecommunications, consumer protection, and emerging technology.\n\n \n\nWe move quickly and expect our lawyers to be practical, proactive, and business-minded. You will not be limited to a narrow legal lane. Instead, you will be expected to understand the company’s products, customers, commercial goals, and regulatory environment, and to help craft thoughtful, scalable solutions. This is a role for someone who wants to become a true partner to business leadership and help shape the legal strategy of a company building the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nWhat you’ll do\n\n - Draft, review, negotiate, and manage a wide range of commercial agreements, including SaaS agreements, MSAs, SOWs, order forms, NDAs, DPAs, vendor agreements, distribution agreements, partnership agreements, and other strategic commercial contracts\n\n - Partner closely with business leadership, product, operations, and finance to support enterprise deals and strategic initiatives\n\n - Advise on product development and product launches, including identifying legal risks and developing practical, business-oriented solutions\n\n - Develop expertise in new and evolving legal areas relevant to Vetcove’s business, including telecommunications, consumer protection, privacy, FDA, DEA, veterinary practice laws, pharmacy laws, ecommerce, marketplace regulation, and related compliance frameworks\n\n - Help translate complex legal and regulatory requirements into practical guidance for product, engineering, operations, and business teams\n\n - Support strategic growth initiatives, including new products, new markets, new commercial models, and new regulated workflows\n\n \n\nWhat you should have\n\n - 5-8 years of legal experience, including experience at a top-tier law firm\n\n - J.D. from an accredited law school and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar\n\n - Strong commercial contracting experience, particularly with SaaS, technology, enterprise customers, MSAs, SOWs, order forms, DPAs, vendor agreements, and related commercial agreements\n\n - Excellent drafting, negotiation, and issue-spotting skills\n\n - Exceptional attention to detail\n\n - Very strong work ethic and desire to dive deeply into the business\n\n - Experience advising high-growth technology companies, SaaS businesses, regulated businesses, or enterprise software companies\n\n - Curiosity and enthusiasm for learning new and evolving regulatory frameworks, and translating them into practical guidance for the business team\n\n - A proactive, ownership-oriented mindset and a strong desire to solve problems rather than simply identify them\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set-up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $180,000/year - $230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There may be a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000-$230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects base annual compensation and does not include bonus, equity, or other incentives.\n\n \n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits package. Please refer to the “Benefits” section above for more details.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bc5ec53c-b1e3-4154-bf4a-f6f27889904f","title":"Senior Software Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:08:16.468+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/bc5ec53c-b1e3-4154-bf4a-f6f27889904f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/bc5ec53c-b1e3-4154-bf4a-f6f27889904f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Software Engineer Role is a key member of our engineering team who is responsible for supporting projects from conception to completion. This level of involvement includes plan formulation, creation, maintenance and upgrade implementations across most of the technology stack. As a contributor to the core features of the Vetcove platform, you will be an integral part of ensuring we are creating intuitive and innovative products that our users need for success in their day to day.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About our team</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe every engineer at Vetcove should have a holistic view of Vetcove and work on many areas of our technology stack. We encourage you to apply to help us grow a system that facilitates billions of dollars in orders each year. We move lightning-fast in an industry that was previously slow to adopt technology. As Vetcove quickly expands its offerings to better serve veterinary groups and its supply chain partners, we’re quickly growing our engineering team to keep pace with the rapid expansion of our business, while maintaining exceptional code quality and system integrity.  You’ll have an opportunity to work closely with end users, handle large scale infrastructure challenges, and everything in between. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving, highly collaborative team!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Some projects we've worked on recently</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A real time analytics platform to display billions of dollars in purchase history</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A dynamic advertising platform that gives away millions of dollars in cash back rewards to clinics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A mobile shopping experience that lets clinic shop using their phone’s camera</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Laid the foundation for a new, modern architecture to support seamless interactivity between several major features</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the conceptualization and feature documentation of new ideas and product enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and extend interactive React applications that will be used by tens of thousands of veterinary purchasers, corporate hospital groups owners, and animal health manufacturers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Add good test coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building reusable components for use by the larger team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement new features into our React Native applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with our CTO and engineering team, as well as across other functions to continuously evolve our platform and products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2 years of professional software engineering experience, (preferably building web applications)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree required, ideally in Computer Science </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High proficiency over at least one industry-common language and be conversant (and interested to improve!) in others</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in building a professionally successful production application in a modern web framework </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to design new features around data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with a database and analyzing queries for improved optimizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with JavaScript’s features as a prototyped and functional language</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good software testing habits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to help our customers succeed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with a backend language, an ORM, and writing API endpoints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup work experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a remote environment </p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tools we use</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Backend: </strong>Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Frontend: </strong>JavaScript (React, Redux), Less.js, Typescript, Webpack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Datastores: </strong>Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mobile: </strong>React Native</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Version Control: </strong>Git</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $115,000/year - $180,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $130,000 - $170,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position \n\nThe Senior Software Engineer Role is a key member of our engineering team who is responsible for supporting projects from conception to completion. This level of involvement includes plan formulation, creation, maintenance and upgrade implementations across most of the technology stack. As a contributor to the core features of the Vetcove platform, you will be an integral part of ensuring we are creating intuitive and innovative products that our users need for success in their day to day.\n\n \n\nAbout our team\n\nWe believe every engineer at Vetcove should have a holistic view of Vetcove and work on many areas of our technology stack. We encourage you to apply to help us grow a system that facilitates billions of dollars in orders each year. We move lightning-fast in an industry that was previously slow to adopt technology. As Vetcove quickly expands its offerings to better serve veterinary groups and its supply chain partners, we’re quickly growing our engineering team to keep pace with the rapid expansion of our business, while maintaining exceptional code quality and system integrity.  You’ll have an opportunity to work closely with end users, handle large scale infrastructure challenges, and everything in between. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving, highly collaborative team!\n\n \n\nSome projects we've worked on recently\n\n - A real time analytics platform to display billions of dollars in purchase history\n\n - A dynamic advertising platform that gives away millions of dollars in cash back rewards to clinics\n\n - A mobile shopping experience that lets clinic shop using their phone’s camera\n\n - Laid the foundation for a new, modern architecture to support seamless interactivity between several major features\n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Contribute to the conceptualization and feature documentation of new ideas and product enhancements\n\n - Build and extend interactive React applications that will be used by tens of thousands of veterinary purchasers, corporate hospital groups owners, and animal health manufacturers\n\n - Add good test coverage\n\n - Building reusable components for use by the larger team\n\n - Implement new features into our React Native applications\n\n - Work directly with our CTO and engineering team, as well as across other functions to continuously evolve our platform and products\n\n - Work in a fully remote environment\n\n \n\nWhat you should have\n\n - 2 years of professional software engineering experience, (preferably building web applications)\n\n - Bachelor's Degree required, ideally in Computer Science \n\n - High proficiency over at least one industry-common language and be conversant (and interested to improve!) in others\n\n - Experience in building a professionally successful production application in a modern web framework \n\n - Ability to design new features around data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind\n\n - Experience working with a database and analyzing queries for improved optimizations\n\n - Fluency with JavaScript’s features as a prototyped and functional language\n\n - Good software testing habits\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities\n\n - A strong desire to help our customers succeed\n\n - A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality\n\n - Experience working with a backend language, an ORM, and writing API endpoints\n\n - Startup work experience is a plus\n\n - Comfortable working in a remote environment \n\n \n\nTools we use\n\n - Backend: Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)\n\n - Frontend: JavaScript (React, Redux), Less.js, Typescript, Webpack\n\n - Datastores: Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis\n\n - Mobile: React Native\n\n - Version Control: Git\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $115,000/year - $180,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $130,000 - $170,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. \n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e76a2aa4-fc2c-4150-8e36-4ba3e43be06a","title":"Account Manager-Customer Success","department":"Account Management ","team":"Account Management ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:25:36.053+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/e76a2aa4-fc2c-4150-8e36-4ba3e43be06a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/e76a2aa4-fc2c-4150-8e36-4ba3e43be06a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What You'll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the main point of contact for all client day-to-day communication and oversight, while also acting in a customer success capacity, being a long term strategic advisor to clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craft agendas, host weekly meetings, and stay on top of actions items for key accounts </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with cross-functional counterparts to ensure you’re up to speed on the latest business initiatives for the Vetcove product and can communicate such initiatives to clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Project manage catalog updates, marketing campaigns, and ad hoc reporting requests for key accounts </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze account performance and create presentations to deliver performance updates and optimization opportunities to key stakeholders </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with product and engineering on client feedback loop, bug identification and resolutions </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with onboarding and implementation to on-board new acquisition clinics </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nurture Corporate relationships to drive affinity, loyalty, and trust in the Vetcove HD platform </p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>You Should Have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+  years of experience in account management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills; comfortable in front of Senior leadership contacts </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent time and process management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in developing client facing reports with actionable insights and recommendations </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in developing and presenting data analyses and partner business reviews </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of entire Microsoft Office suite, with an emphasis on PowerPoint and Excel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in client relationship building and willingness to travel for client-facing events </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $110,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $85,000 - $100,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Be the main point of contact for all client day-to-day communication and oversight, while also acting in a customer success capacity, being a long term strategic advisor to clients\n\n - Craft agendas, host weekly meetings, and stay on top of actions items for key accounts \n\n - Collaborate with cross-functional counterparts to ensure you’re up to speed on the latest business initiatives for the Vetcove product and can communicate such initiatives to clients\n\n - Project manage catalog updates, marketing campaigns, and ad hoc reporting requests for key accounts \n\n - Analyze account performance and create presentations to deliver performance updates and optimization opportunities to key stakeholders \n\n - Work with product and engineering on client feedback loop, bug identification and resolutions \n\n - Work with onboarding and implementation to on-board new acquisition clinics \n\n - Nurture Corporate relationships to drive affinity, loyalty, and trust in the Vetcove HD platform \n\n \n\n\nYOU SHOULD HAVE\n\n - 4+  years of experience in account management\n\n - Bachelor's Degree\n\n - Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills; comfortable in front of Senior leadership contacts \n\n - Excellent time and process management skills\n\n - Experience in developing client facing reports with actionable insights and recommendations \n\n - Experience in developing and presenting data analyses and partner business reviews \n\n - Strong working knowledge of entire Microsoft Office suite, with an emphasis on PowerPoint and Excel\n\n - Interest in client relationship building and willingness to travel for client-facing events \n\n - A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $110,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $85,000 - $100,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0f68b3ac-56f1-4b6b-955d-bbae30a8d698","title":"General Manager, B2B Marketplace (VP-Level)","department":"Sales and Retention","team":"Sales and Retention","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:56:13.438+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/0f68b3ac-56f1-4b6b-955d-bbae30a8d698","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/0f68b3ac-56f1-4b6b-955d-bbae30a8d698/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The General Manager of the Clinic Purchasing Platform is responsible for the performance and operations of Vetcove's flagship purchasing platform and many of the company's most important enterprise customer relationships.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will lead the teams responsible for Account Management and Customer Experience, overseeing a combined organization of approximately 15 customer-facing professionals through two experienced managers. Together, these teams support Vetcove's largest corporate customers, driving adoption, retention, operational excellence, and long-term partner success.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be accountable for the success of Vetcove's largest enterprise partners. That means understanding their business, identifying opportunities to deepen each relationship, coordinating execution across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, and Operations, and ensuring Vetcove consistently delivers on its commitments.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a highly cross-functional leadership role that combines operational execution, people leadership, and commercial strategy. You'll be responsible for developing your managers, scaling the organization as the business grows, and ensuring Vetcove continues to deliver an exceptional experience on this platform.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the performance and operations of Vetcove's Clinic Purchasing Platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop two experienced managers responsible for Account Management and Customer Experience, overseeing a combined organization of approximately 15 customer-facing professionals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, and Operations to prioritize customer needs and drive cross-functional initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather customer and market feedback to help inform commercial strategy, product direction, and long-term investment decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and provide guidance on executive-facing customer materials, including proposals, business reviews, strategic plans, and performance updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously improve the processes, metrics, and operating rhythms used by the Account Management and Customer Experience organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct regular business reviews with your managers to evaluate account health, identify opportunities and risks, and ensure teams are executing against priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Travel up to 25% to meet with enterprise customers for strategic planning sessions, business reviews, and executive relationship building.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of account management, relationship-based sales, or similar experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous people management responsibilities, including experience managing managers or leading teams through other leaders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience managing complex enterprise relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An eagerness to be involved in the details of ongoing projects, despite a high-level role &amp; title</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and project management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in data and more quantitative problem solving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in Excel, PowerPoint, and Word</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and team-based mentality; excellent collaboration skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortability in a fast-paced environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $280,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1,2026.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nThe General Manager of the Clinic Purchasing Platform is responsible for the performance and operations of Vetcove's flagship purchasing platform and many of the company's most important enterprise customer relationships.\n\n \n\nYou will lead the teams responsible for Account Management and Customer Experience, overseeing a combined organization of approximately 15 customer-facing professionals through two experienced managers. Together, these teams support Vetcove's largest corporate customers, driving adoption, retention, operational excellence, and long-term partner success.\n\n \n\nYou will be accountable for the success of Vetcove's largest enterprise partners. That means understanding their business, identifying opportunities to deepen each relationship, coordinating execution across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, and Operations, and ensuring Vetcove consistently delivers on its commitments.\n\n \n\nThis is a highly cross-functional leadership role that combines operational execution, people leadership, and commercial strategy. You'll be responsible for developing your managers, scaling the organization as the business grows, and ensuring Vetcove continues to deliver an exceptional experience on this platform.\n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Own the performance and operations of Vetcove's Clinic Purchasing Platform\n\n - Lead and develop two experienced managers responsible for Account Management and Customer Experience, overseeing a combined organization of approximately 15 customer-facing professionals.\n\n - Partner with Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, and Operations to prioritize customer needs and drive cross-functional initiatives.\n\n - Gather customer and market feedback to help inform commercial strategy, product direction, and long-term investment decisions.\n\n - Review and provide guidance on executive-facing customer materials, including proposals, business reviews, strategic plans, and performance updates.\n\n - Continuously improve the processes, metrics, and operating rhythms used by the Account Management and Customer Experience organizations.\n\n - Conduct regular business reviews with your managers to evaluate account health, identify opportunities and risks, and ensure teams are executing against priorities.\n\n - Travel up to 25% to meet with enterprise customers for strategic planning sessions, business reviews, and executive relationship building.\n\n \n\nYou should have\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 8+ years of account management, relationship-based sales, or similar experience\n\n - Previous people management responsibilities, including experience managing managers or leading teams through other leaders\n\n - Proven experience managing complex enterprise relationships\n\n - An eagerness to be involved in the details of ongoing projects, despite a high-level role & title\n\n - Strong attention to detail and project management skills\n\n - Interest in data and more quantitative problem solving\n\n - Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities\n\n - Expertise in Excel, PowerPoint, and Word\n\n - A positive attitude and team-based mentality; excellent collaboration skills\n\n - Comfortability in a fast-paced environment\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $280,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $180,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1,2026.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1ec4c8d3-baa2-4282-8c0c-8474d9d1605a","title":"Recruiter","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:09:34.731+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/1ec4c8d3-baa2-4282-8c0c-8474d9d1605a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/1ec4c8d3-baa2-4282-8c0c-8474d9d1605a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Recruiter to help us attract, engage, and hire exceptional  talent at Vetcove. You’ll be the engine driving our recruiting and sourcing strategy — from uncovering hard-to-find candidates to guiding them through the process and ensuring a world-class candidate experience.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll partner closely with leadership, the cofounders, and hiring managers to build an effective and scalable hiring pipeline. You’ll lead sourcing initiatives, refine recruiting processes, and work with a small but mighty team focused on filling our most critical roles.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>What You’ll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and evolve our <strong>recruiting strategy</strong> across all teams </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with leadership and hiring managers to deeply understand needs and design targeted hiring plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain proactive sourcing pipelines for both active and passive candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement creative, data-driven sourcing strategies for hard-to-fill positions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and report recruiting metrics, ensuring clear visibility into pipeline health and performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize and manage recruiting tools and systems (e.g., ATS, sourcing platforms).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion the candidate experience, from first touch to offer close</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to employer branding efforts to elevate our presence in the technical talent market</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>You Should Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of recruiting experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success sourcing and closing candidates for technical and non-technical </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong track record in fast-paced, scaling environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in building and optimizing recruiting pipelines and processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills and the ability to partner effectively with executives and hiring managers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with ATS systems and technical sourcing tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly analytical with a bias toward action and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in an environment with evolving priorities and ambiguity</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Benefits (Full-Time Roles)</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At-home office setup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $70,000/year - $135,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $70,000 - $125,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nWe’re looking for a Recruiter to help us attract, engage, and hire exceptional  talent at Vetcove. You’ll be the engine driving our recruiting and sourcing strategy — from uncovering hard-to-find candidates to guiding them through the process and ensuring a world-class candidate experience.\n\n \n\nIn this role, you’ll partner closely with leadership, the cofounders, and hiring managers to build an effective and scalable hiring pipeline. You’ll lead sourcing initiatives, refine recruiting processes, and work with a small but mighty team focused on filling our most critical roles.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own and evolve our recruiting strategy across all teams \n\n - Partner with leadership and hiring managers to deeply understand needs and design targeted hiring plans\n\n - Build and maintain proactive sourcing pipelines for both active and passive candidates\n\n - Implement creative, data-driven sourcing strategies for hard-to-fill positions\n\n - Track and report recruiting metrics, ensuring clear visibility into pipeline health and performance\n\n - Optimize and manage recruiting tools and systems (e.g., ATS, sourcing platforms).\n\n - Champion the candidate experience, from first touch to offer close\n\n - Contribute to employer branding efforts to elevate our presence in the technical talent market\n\n \n\n\nYOU SHOULD HAVE\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 3+ years of recruiting experience\n\n - Proven success sourcing and closing candidates for technical and non-technical \n\n - Strong track record in fast-paced, scaling environments\n\n - Expertise in building and optimizing recruiting pipelines and processes\n\n - Exceptional communication skills and the ability to partner effectively with executives and hiring managers\n\n - Proficiency with ATS systems and technical sourcing tools\n\n - Highly analytical with a bias toward action and iteration\n\n - Comfortable working in an environment with evolving priorities and ambiguity\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL-TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At-home office setup\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $70,000/year - $135,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $70,000 - $125,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an ongoing basis.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cfe17c78-f43b-4004-af29-32c05df6af66","title":"Senior Account Manager-Customer Success","department":"Account Management ","team":"Account Management ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:04:22.326+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/cfe17c78-f43b-4004-af29-32c05df6af66","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/cfe17c78-f43b-4004-af29-32c05df6af66/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is looking for a Senior Account Manager. As the veterinary market continues to consolidate, we’re looking for someone to develop, maintain, and grow our relationships with the key veterinary hospital consolidators. You’ll be leading all of our efforts in this aspect of the business.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Account Manager you will be responsible for working directly with our existing network of corporate hospital group partners to understand their developing needs and react to them in order to inform both our long-term company strategy and product development roadmap. In addition to working with our current accounts, you will be developing strategic relationships with many others to strengthen our competitive position among the largest veterinary consolidators.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will serve as the primary point of contact, and trusted partner, working with our corporate partners (and future partners) to fully understand their needs, demonstrate our value, and ensure we’re strategically positioned to best support them.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the main point of contact for all day-to-day client communication and oversight, while also acting in a customer success capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and lead Vetcove’s corporate accounts strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Position yourself as a strategic partner to key stakeholders and champions within named accounts in order to build and maintain strong, long-lasting relationships </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craft narratives and prove customer value through comprehensive business reviews and strategic touch-points, both over the phone and through on-site meetings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop proficiency in collecting ongoing customer product feedback to establish an effective feedback loop for customer needs and our product development strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take a methodical approach to strategic planning in each of your owned accounts by creating a roadmap which continuously progresses the customer towards their specific platform goals, account growth, and overall success with Vetcove</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay tuned in to the veterinary consolidation market and understand how Vetcove can evolve to adapt to changes in market dynamics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nurture relationships with non-contracted corporate consolidators to be sure they understand Vetcove’s value and how we can fit into long term strategy</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>You should have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years in account management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent time and process management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success identifying and developing executive relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $100,000/year - $150,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $100,000 - $120,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the position\n\nVetcove is looking for a Senior Account Manager. As the veterinary market continues to consolidate, we’re looking for someone to develop, maintain, and grow our relationships with the key veterinary hospital consolidators. You’ll be leading all of our efforts in this aspect of the business.\n\n \n\nAs a Senior Account Manager you will be responsible for working directly with our existing network of corporate hospital group partners to understand their developing needs and react to them in order to inform both our long-term company strategy and product development roadmap. In addition to working with our current accounts, you will be developing strategic relationships with many others to strengthen our competitive position among the largest veterinary consolidators.\n\n \n\nYou will serve as the primary point of contact, and trusted partner, working with our corporate partners (and future partners) to fully understand their needs, demonstrate our value, and ensure we’re strategically positioned to best support them.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Serve as the main point of contact for all day-to-day client communication and oversight, while also acting in a customer success capacity\n\n - Design and lead Vetcove’s corporate accounts strategy\n\n - Position yourself as a strategic partner to key stakeholders and champions within named accounts in order to build and maintain strong, long-lasting relationships \n\n - Craft narratives and prove customer value through comprehensive business reviews and strategic touch-points, both over the phone and through on-site meetings\n\n - Develop proficiency in collecting ongoing customer product feedback to establish an effective feedback loop for customer needs and our product development strategy\n\n - Take a methodical approach to strategic planning in each of your owned accounts by creating a roadmap which continuously progresses the customer towards their specific platform goals, account growth, and overall success with Vetcove\n\n - Stay tuned in to the veterinary consolidation market and understand how Vetcove can evolve to adapt to changes in market dynamics\n\n - Nurture relationships with non-contracted corporate consolidators to be sure they understand Vetcove’s value and how we can fit into long term strategy\n\n \n\n\nYOU SHOULD HAVE\n\n - Bachelors Degree \n\n - 8+ years in account management\n\n - Exceptional verbal, written, and presentation skills\n\n - Excellent time and process management skills\n\n - Strong analytical skills \n\n - Proven success identifying and developing executive relationships\n\n - A strong desire to learn and define an emerging function in a rapidly growing and dynamic startup environment\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $100,000/year - $150,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $100,000 - $120,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5825a644-8a0c-4104-9d61-688a8d968108","title":"Staff Product Designer","department":"Design","team":"Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:58:08.738+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/5825a644-8a0c-4104-9d61-688a8d968108","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/5825a644-8a0c-4104-9d61-688a8d968108/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is looking for an experienced and versatile staff product designer to help us craft exceptional experiences that empower veterinary clinics to thrive.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a designer at Vetcove, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the tools that clinics use every day to run their practices, from inventory management to pharmacy workflows and beyond. You’ll own design efforts end-to-end—from early discovery and research to wireframes and polished visuals—collaborating closely with engineers, PMs, and our founding team along the way. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone who can think in systems, prototype ideas quickly, and bring clarity to complex workflows. You’ll be instrumental in shaping not only our product, but our overall design culture as we scale. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a <em>fast-moving</em>, highly collaborative team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead end-to-end design for core product areas—taking ideas from early concept to final implementation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product managers and engineers to define team roadmaps and ensure we’re solving the right problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with engineers to ensure a high-quality implementation that matches the design intent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create flows, wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes to communicate design ideas clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate design sprints, user research sessions, and collaborative workshops</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help evolve and maintain our design system to ensure a cohesive experience across the platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in a fully remote environment! </p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 5+ years of experience designing thoughtful, intuitive web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve shipped complex B2B or SaaS products, and can speak to your process in doing so</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think in systems and patterns, and have strong instincts for usability, interaction design, and hierarchy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You move fluidly between user experience, interaction, and visual design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong portfolio that shows off your product thinking and attention to detail<br />You thrive in fast-paced, collaborative environments and enjoy working closely with engineers and stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You care deeply about quality and craftsmanship—but you’re also pragmatic when needed</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $120,000/year -$210,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $130,000 - $190,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nVetcove is looking for an experienced and versatile staff product designer to help us craft exceptional experiences that empower veterinary clinics to thrive.\n\n \n\nAs a designer at Vetcove, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the tools that clinics use every day to run their practices, from inventory management to pharmacy workflows and beyond. You’ll own design efforts end-to-end—from early discovery and research to wireframes and polished visuals—collaborating closely with engineers, PMs, and our founding team along the way. \n\n \n\nWe’re looking for someone who can think in systems, prototype ideas quickly, and bring clarity to complex workflows. You’ll be instrumental in shaping not only our product, but our overall design culture as we scale. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast-moving, highly collaborative team.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Lead end-to-end design for core product areas—taking ideas from early concept to final implementation\n\n - Collaborate with product managers and engineers to define team roadmaps and ensure we’re solving the right problems\n\n - Partner with engineers to ensure a high-quality implementation that matches the design intent\n\n - Create flows, wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes to communicate design ideas clearly\n\n - Facilitate design sprints, user research sessions, and collaborative workshops\n\n - Help evolve and maintain our design system to ensure a cohesive experience across the platform\n\n - Work in a fully remote environment! \n\n \n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You have 5+ years of experience designing thoughtful, intuitive web applications\n\n - You’ve shipped complex B2B or SaaS products, and can speak to your process in doing so\n\n - You think in systems and patterns, and have strong instincts for usability, interaction design, and hierarchy\n\n - You move fluidly between user experience, interaction, and visual design\n\n - You have a strong portfolio that shows off your product thinking and attention to detail\n   You thrive in fast-paced, collaborative environments and enjoy working closely with engineers and stakeholders\n\n - You care deeply about quality and craftsmanship—but you’re also pragmatic when needed\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $120,000/year -$210,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $130,000 - $190,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails. To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis. \n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"30e11d83-38f7-442a-a207-46a4dbe7f54a","title":"Vet Clinic Retention Associate","department":"Sales and Retention","team":"Sales and Retention","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:04:01.637+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/30e11d83-38f7-442a-a207-46a4dbe7f54a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/30e11d83-38f7-442a-a207-46a4dbe7f54a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Customer Retention team is responsible for maintaining and strengthening existing relationships with our vibrant community of veterinary professionals! The Customer Retention team uses a multifaceted approach to identify weak spots in our relationships with customers, as well as field objections and concerns so that we can work towards a resolution and stronger relationship. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is achieved through a variety of holistic methods including strategic outbound calling, community events, educational courses &amp; webinars, an ambassador program, email campaigns, reporting, and collaborative content. This role constitutes a vital piece of the overall customer experience journey, so candidates will work closely with both the Customer Experience team as well as the Sales &amp; Growth team. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of proactively engaging with our customer base and is willing to go the extra mile to ensure all concerns are addressed. Candidates are expected to engage with a large (and quickly growing) community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals by phone, live chat, email, and video conference. The ideal candidate has a passion for helping others and is empathetic, resilient, and tenacious. </p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategically identify clinics who may be slipping away as an active customer </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform proactive outreach to clinics predominantly via phone in addition to email, live chat, and video conference</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Train, educate, and develop existing Vetcove users so they may engage on the Vetcove platform more deeply and meaningfully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Field concerns and objections in a level-headed and compassionate manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create engaging content that educates and supports all veterinary professionals, including doctors, veterinary technicians, and inventory specialists </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage in highly analytical and critical thinking to best understand the flow of clinics in and out of our active user base </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solicit feedback from our customers in order to understand how we can better evolve our platform and proactively field any objections clinics may have to using Vetcove</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally to provide our customer experience team, sales and growth team, as well as our engineering team with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline customer retention workflows and strategies</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You should have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-3 years of relevant, customer facing work experience </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong desire to help our customers succeed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to give highly engaging presentations and demos </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience on tech platforms a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Veterinary Industry experience strongly preferred</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $50,000/year - $75,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $55,000 - $70,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position \n\nThe Customer Retention team is responsible for maintaining and strengthening existing relationships with our vibrant community of veterinary professionals! The Customer Retention team uses a multifaceted approach to identify weak spots in our relationships with customers, as well as field objections and concerns so that we can work towards a resolution and stronger relationship. \n\n \n\nThis is achieved through a variety of holistic methods including strategic outbound calling, community events, educational courses & webinars, an ambassador program, email campaigns, reporting, and collaborative content. This role constitutes a vital piece of the overall customer experience journey, so candidates will work closely with both the Customer Experience team as well as the Sales & Growth team. \n\n \n\nThe ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who thrives in a team environment. This person will be excited by the challenge of proactively engaging with our customer base and is willing to go the extra mile to ensure all concerns are addressed. Candidates are expected to engage with a large (and quickly growing) community of thousands of passionate veterinary professionals by phone, live chat, email, and video conference. The ideal candidate has a passion for helping others and is empathetic, resilient, and tenacious. \n\n \n\nWhat you'll do\n\n - Strategically identify clinics who may be slipping away as an active customer \n\n - Perform proactive outreach to clinics predominantly via phone in addition to email, live chat, and video conference\n\n - Train, educate, and develop existing Vetcove users so they may engage on the Vetcove platform more deeply and meaningfully\n\n - Field concerns and objections in a level-headed and compassionate manner\n\n - Create engaging content that educates and supports all veterinary professionals, including doctors, veterinary technicians, and inventory specialists \n\n - Engage in highly analytical and critical thinking to best understand the flow of clinics in and out of our active user base \n\n - Solicit feedback from our customers in order to understand how we can better evolve our platform and proactively field any objections clinics may have to using Vetcove\n\n - Work cross-functionally to provide our customer experience team, sales and growth team, as well as our engineering team with information on feature requests and recommendations for enhancements to our tools \n\n - Help to continuously develop and expand processes in order to streamline customer retention workflows and strategies\n\n \n\nYou should have\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 1-3 years of relevant, customer facing work experience \n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Ability to adapt quickly and manage many concurrent responsibilities\n\n - A strong desire to help our customers succeed\n\n - A positive attitude and one-for-all team mentality\n\n - Ability to give highly engaging presentations and demos \n\n - Experience on tech platforms a plus\n\n - Veterinary Industry experience strongly preferred\n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $50,000/year - $75,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $55,000 - $70,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is October 1st, 2026.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fbd33d4b-7a73-46c2-9707-525c8130e2fa","title":"Clinic Growth Manager","department":"Sales and Retention","team":"Sales and Retention","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:39:23.300+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/fbd33d4b-7a73-46c2-9707-525c8130e2fa","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/fbd33d4b-7a73-46c2-9707-525c8130e2fa/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Clinic Growth Manager you'll design and run the programs that keep thousands of veterinary clinics engaged, growing, and getting real value from Vetcove – and you'll know how to identify the ones who need a personal nudge and go get them.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll think in programs, not just conversations – using data, content, and community to move thousands of clinics at once.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and manage a clinic community program including newsletters, referral programs, peer spotlights, and online engagement initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and run clinic-focused seminars and educational webinars on topics like in-platform best practices, successful workflows, and platform updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop best practice playbooks, how-to guides, and self-serve resources that help clinics maximize platform value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead best practice sessions to share learnings, tips, and platform updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze usage trends, sales patterns, and platform engagement to identify underperforming clinics and build targeted re-engagement plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor key health metrics across the platform to flag at-risk accounts before churn becomes a risk</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a feedback loop between clinics and the product team: know what clinics need and advocate for it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools and partnership with the data team to build and maintain dashboards to track clinic health, engagement, and growth metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare regular business reviews with data-driven insights for internal stakeholders</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of experience in Community Engagement, Growth Marketing, Customer Success, Account Management, or a client-facing role, ideally in a SaaS or technology company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of driving measurable growth outcomes across a large customer base</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with data: You can pull a report, spot a trend, and translate it into action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or contributing to community programs, event coordination, or customer education initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A natural communicator who can hold a room in a seminar, build trust in a 1:1, and write a newsletter people actually read</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple programs and initiatives simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable shifting between program-level thinking and direct clinic conversations when the situation calls for it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skilled at translating user feedback and behavioral data into program decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in veterinary, healthcare, or life sciences is a strong plus but not required</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Haves</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar CRM tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with customer health scoring or churn prediction frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a high-growth startup environment</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $140,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $130,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\nAs a Clinic Growth Manager you'll design and run the programs that keep thousands of veterinary clinics engaged, growing, and getting real value from Vetcove – and you'll know how to identify the ones who need a personal nudge and go get them.\n\n \n\nYou'll think in programs, not just conversations – using data, content, and community to move thousands of clinics at once.\n\n \n\nWhat You Will Do\n\n - Design and manage a clinic community program including newsletters, referral programs, peer spotlights, and online engagement initiatives\n\n - Develop and run clinic-focused seminars and educational webinars on topics like in-platform best practices, successful workflows, and platform updates\n\n - Develop best practice playbooks, how-to guides, and self-serve resources that help clinics maximize platform value\n\n - Lead best practice sessions to share learnings, tips, and platform updates\n\n - Analyze usage trends, sales patterns, and platform engagement to identify underperforming clinics and build targeted re-engagement plans\n\n - Monitor key health metrics across the platform to flag at-risk accounts before churn becomes a risk\n\n - Act as a feedback loop between clinics and the product team: know what clinics need and advocate for it\n\n - Leverage AI tools and partnership with the data team to build and maintain dashboards to track clinic health, engagement, and growth metrics\n\n - Prepare regular business reviews with data-driven insights for internal stakeholders\n\n \n\nWhat We’re Looking For\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 3–5 years of experience in Community Engagement, Growth Marketing, Customer Success, Account Management, or a client-facing role, ideally in a SaaS or technology company\n\n - A track record of driving measurable growth outcomes across a large customer base\n\n - Comfort with data: You can pull a report, spot a trend, and translate it into action\n\n - Experience building or contributing to community programs, event coordination, or customer education initiatives\n\n - A natural communicator who can hold a room in a seminar, build trust in a 1:1, and write a newsletter people actually read\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple programs and initiatives simultaneously\n\n - Comfortable shifting between program-level thinking and direct clinic conversations when the situation calls for it.\n\n - Skilled at translating user feedback and behavioral data into program decisions\n\n - Experience in veterinary, healthcare, or life sciences is a strong plus but not required\n\n \n\nNice to Haves\n\n - Familiarity with Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar CRM tools\n\n - Experience with customer health scoring or churn prediction frameworks\n\n - Prior experience in a high-growth startup environment\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $80,000/year - $140,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $130,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b6f9c7a2-c260-45ab-9114-a60bd48025a4","title":"Manager, Client Onboarding and Implementation","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T14:59:15.680+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/b6f9c7a2-c260-45ab-9114-a60bd48025a4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/b6f9c7a2-c260-45ab-9114-a60bd48025a4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Onboarding and Implementation Manager at Vetcove, you'll lead the strategy and execution of end-to-end onboarding for veterinary clinics across our platform. You'll manage and mentor a team of 5+ Onboarding Specialists, setting the standard for how clinics experience implementation—from kickoff through post-launch—while ensuring every clinic is positioned for long-term success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll serve as the point of contact for clinic partnerships during implementation, drive cross-functional alignment with product, engineering, strategy, and support, and build the systems and processes that allow your team to scale. In some cases, you may travel to client sites to support critical go-lives and ensure successful deployment.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, coach, and develop a team of 5+ Onboarding Specialists, driving accountability and a high standard of client delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the overall implementation strategy and lifecycle—from project planning frameworks to go-live execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the escalation point and key liaison between veterinary clinics and internal teams, ensuring a seamless and consultative onboarding experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define team-wide project goals, success metrics, and delivery standards aligned with client needs and business priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide clinics through complex migrations of existing workflows onto a new platform, providing both strategic direction and hands-on support where needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, refine, and scale project management processes, templates, and tooling used across the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee training delivery and support your team in troubleshooting configuration, data imports, and integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain clear, executive-level communication with internal stakeholders and client leadership to ensure transparency and alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering to influence the implementation workflow and champion the needs of clients and your team</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You Should Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years managing complex software implementation projects, preferably in a SaaS or tech-enabled services environment, with at least 2 years in a people management role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience leading and developing high-performing teams in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage team capacity across multiple concurrent client engagements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills with both technical and non-technical audiences, including executive stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in project management tools and experience building scalable processes, timelines, and reporting frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with clinics, healthcare providers, or other medical environments is a plus but not required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel to client sites as needed (up to 10–15%)</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $90,000/year - $150,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $120,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\nAs an Onboarding and Implementation Manager at Vetcove, you'll lead the strategy and execution of end-to-end onboarding for veterinary clinics across our platform. You'll manage and mentor a team of 5+ Onboarding Specialists, setting the standard for how clinics experience implementation—from kickoff through post-launch—while ensuring every clinic is positioned for long-term success.\n\nYou'll serve as the point of contact for clinic partnerships during implementation, drive cross-functional alignment with product, engineering, strategy, and support, and build the systems and processes that allow your team to scale. In some cases, you may travel to client sites to support critical go-lives and ensure successful deployment.\n\n \n\nWhat You'll Do\n\n - Lead, coach, and develop a team of 5+ Onboarding Specialists, driving accountability and a high standard of client delivery\n\n - Own the overall implementation strategy and lifecycle—from project planning frameworks to go-live execution\n\n - Serve as the escalation point and key liaison between veterinary clinics and internal teams, ensuring a seamless and consultative onboarding experience\n\n - Define team-wide project goals, success metrics, and delivery standards aligned with client needs and business priorities\n\n - Guide clinics through complex migrations of existing workflows onto a new platform, providing both strategic direction and hands-on support where needed\n\n - Build, refine, and scale project management processes, templates, and tooling used across the team\n\n - Oversee training delivery and support your team in troubleshooting configuration, data imports, and integrations\n\n - Maintain clear, executive-level communication with internal stakeholders and client leadership to ensure transparency and alignment\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering to influence the implementation workflow and champion the needs of clients and your team\n\n \n\nYou Should Have\n\n - Bachelor's degree \n\n - 4+ years managing complex software implementation projects, preferably in a SaaS or tech-enabled services environment, with at least 2 years in a people management role\n\n - Proven experience leading and developing high-performing teams in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage team capacity across multiple concurrent client engagements\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication skills with both technical and non-technical audiences, including executive stakeholders\n\n - Proficiency in project management tools and experience building scalable processes, timelines, and reporting frameworks\n\n - Experience working with clinics, healthcare providers, or other medical environments is a plus but not required\n\n - Willingness to travel to client sites as needed (up to 10–15%)\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $90,000/year - $150,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $90,000 - $120,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"41ed06fc-98fc-479c-8b85-43880ac36788","title":"Staff Software Engineer ","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:01:39.414+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/41ed06fc-98fc-479c-8b85-43880ac36788","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/41ed06fc-98fc-479c-8b85-43880ac36788/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About the Position</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />As a Staff Software Engineer at Vetcove, you’ll take ownership of major product areas—designing, building, and improving the tools that help veterinary clinics streamline operations, deliver exceptional patient care, and optimize their supply chains. The systems you create will manage billions of dollars in transactions and empower clinics to focus on their patients, not their logistics.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn’t just another engineering job—it’s a chance to tackle meaningful challenges and make a real-world impact. You’ll be involved in everything: deciding what to build, designing how it works, and ensuring it gets into the hands of users seamlessly. If you thrive on solving hard problems and creating tools that matter, this role is for you!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>About Our Team</strong></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in a field that’s rapidly adopting technology. Our platform powers every aspect of veterinary clinic operations, from medical records to purchasing workflows. But we’re not just building software—we’re rethinking how the industry operates, making it more efficient and humane.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Vetcove, engineers work across the stack and have a holistic view of the platform. You’ll have the opportunity to work closely with users, influence the product roadmap, and make a real difference in an industry that impacts millions of animals and their caregivers. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving highly collaborative team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design, architecture, and delivery of complex product initiatives across web and mobile platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and enhance React and React Native applications used by tens of thousands of veterinary professionals and industry partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set engineering standards, drive code quality, and ensure strong test coverage across the codebase</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable components, shared libraries, and architectural patterns that support team-wide productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers, provide technical guidance, and influence engineering direction across multiple teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with our CTO, engineering leadership, and cross-functional stakeholders to define and execute high-impact solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design features and data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind, including optimizing database queries and API interactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot complex issues across the stack and lead efforts to improve system performance and reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in a fully remote team environment </p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of professional software engineering experience with ownership of complex, production-grade systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree required, ideally in Computer Science or a related technical field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in at least one modern programming language and strong experience with modern web frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency in JavaScript and React, including architecting large-scale front-end applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to design scalable systems, APIs, and data models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid experience working with relational databases and optimizing queries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent practice of writing well-tested, maintainable, and reliable code</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to mentor engineers and lead technical decision-making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, with the ability to convey complex ideas clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, adaptable, and effective in fast-paced or evolving environments</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Tools We Use</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend: Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontend: JavaScript (React, React-Query), Less.js, TypeScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Datastores: Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis, Clickhouse</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mobile: React Native</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Version Control: Git</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $210,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE POSITION\n\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer at Vetcove, you’ll take ownership of major product areas—designing, building, and improving the tools that help veterinary clinics streamline operations, deliver exceptional patient care, and optimize their supply chains. The systems you create will manage billions of dollars in transactions and empower clinics to focus on their patients, not their logistics.\n\n \n\nThis isn’t just another engineering job—it’s a chance to tackle meaningful challenges and make a real-world impact. You’ll be involved in everything: deciding what to build, designing how it works, and ensuring it gets into the hands of users seamlessly. If you thrive on solving hard problems and creating tools that matter, this role is for you!\n\n \n\n\nABOUT OUR TEAM\n\n \n\nWe’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in a field that’s rapidly adopting technology. Our platform powers every aspect of veterinary clinic operations, from medical records to purchasing workflows. But we’re not just building software—we’re rethinking how the industry operates, making it more efficient and humane.\n\n \n\nAt Vetcove, engineers work across the stack and have a holistic view of the platform. You’ll have the opportunity to work closely with users, influence the product roadmap, and make a real difference in an industry that impacts millions of animals and their caregivers. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast moving highly collaborative team.\n\n \n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Lead the design, architecture, and delivery of complex product initiatives across web and mobile platforms\n\n - Build and enhance React and React Native applications used by tens of thousands of veterinary professionals and industry partners\n\n - Set engineering standards, drive code quality, and ensure strong test coverage across the codebase\n\n - Develop scalable components, shared libraries, and architectural patterns that support team-wide productivity\n\n - Mentor engineers, provide technical guidance, and influence engineering direction across multiple teams\n\n - Partner closely with our CTO, engineering leadership, and cross-functional stakeholders to define and execute high-impact solutions\n\n - Design features and data models with accuracy, security, and performance in mind, including optimizing database queries and API interactions\n\n - Troubleshoot complex issues across the stack and lead efforts to improve system performance and reliability\n\n - Work in a fully remote team environment \n\n \n\nWhat We’re Looking For\n\n - 8+ years of professional software engineering experience with ownership of complex, production-grade systems\n\n - Bachelor’s degree required, ideally in Computer Science or a related technical field\n\n - Deep expertise in at least one modern programming language and strong experience with modern web frameworks\n\n - Strong proficiency in JavaScript and React, including architecting large-scale front-end applications\n\n - Proven ability to design scalable systems, APIs, and data models\n\n - Solid experience working with relational databases and optimizing queries\n\n - Consistent practice of writing well-tested, maintainable, and reliable code\n\n - Demonstrated ability to mentor engineers and lead technical decision-making\n\n - Excellent communication skills, with the ability to convey complex ideas clearly\n\n - Collaborative, adaptable, and effective in fast-paced or evolving environments\n\n \n\n\nTOOLS WE USE\n\n - Backend: Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)\n\n - Frontend: JavaScript (React, React-Query), Less.js, TypeScript\n\n - Datastores: Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis, Clickhouse\n\n - Mobile: React Native\n\n - Version Control: Git\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance  \n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up \n\n - Bi-annual company retreats \n\n - Open vacation policy \n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $230,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits.  There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $210,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\n \n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7c0557ca-fadf-4e6d-8769-c39f87ee5f0d","title":"Staff Frontend Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:12:42.579+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/7c0557ca-fadf-4e6d-8769-c39f87ee5f0d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/7c0557ca-fadf-4e6d-8769-c39f87ee5f0d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Position</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />As a Staff Frontend Engineer, you’ll lead the architecture and evolution of the user facing experience across Vetcove’s platforms. You’ll own critical frontend systems that power how tens of thousands of veterinary professionals and millions of pet parents interact with our products daily; from clinical workflows to patient care tools.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role goes beyond implementation. You’ll define frontend strategy, establish best practices, and shape how our applications scale in performance, usability, and maintainability. You’ll work closely with product, design, and backend teams to deliver seamless, high-quality user experiences at scale.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Our Team</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in a field that’s rapidly adopting technology. Our platform powers every aspect of veterinary clinic operations, from medical records to pet parent experiences. At Vetcove, engineers work across the stack and have a holistic view of the platform. You’ll have the opportunity to work closely with users, influence the product roadmap, and make a real difference in an industry that impacts millions of animals and their caregivers. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast-moving, highly collaborative team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the architecture, design, and delivery of large scale frontend applications across web and mobile</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evolve high performance React and React Native applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and enforce frontend best practices, including performance optimization, accessibility, and maintainability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop shared component libraries, design systems, and frontend infrastructure to improve team velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive improvements in application performance, reliability, and user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product managers, designers, and backend engineers to deliver cohesive, user centered features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor junior front end engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Influence technical direction and frontend strategy across multiple product areas</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Debug and resolve complex frontend and cross stack issues</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of software engineering experience, with a strong focus on frontend development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building Claude/Cursor skills to help streamline FE best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree required, CS or technical degree preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in JavaScript/TypeScript and modern frontend frameworks (especially React)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience architecting and scaling complex frontend applications and systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of performance optimization, state management, and frontend architecture patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and maintaining design systems or shared component libraries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with mobile development (React Native or similar) is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of APIs and backend interactions (REST, GraphQL, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to lead projects and mentor engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and a product-oriented mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating in fast paced, evolving environments</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tools We Use</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend: Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontend: JavaScript (React, React-Query), TypeScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Datastores: Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis, Clickhouse</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mobile: React Native</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Version Control: Git</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $230,000/year + significant bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $220,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />Details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n \n\nAbout the Position\n\n\nAs a Staff Frontend Engineer, you’ll lead the architecture and evolution of the user facing experience across Vetcove’s platforms. You’ll own critical frontend systems that power how tens of thousands of veterinary professionals and millions of pet parents interact with our products daily; from clinical workflows to patient care tools.\n\n \n\nThis role goes beyond implementation. You’ll define frontend strategy, establish best practices, and shape how our applications scale in performance, usability, and maintainability. You’ll work closely with product, design, and backend teams to deliver seamless, high-quality user experiences at scale.\n\n \n\nAbout Our Team\n\n \n\nWe’re a fast-moving team solving big challenges in a field that’s rapidly adopting technology. Our platform powers every aspect of veterinary clinic operations, from medical records to pet parent experiences. At Vetcove, engineers work across the stack and have a holistic view of the platform. You’ll have the opportunity to work closely with users, influence the product roadmap, and make a real difference in an industry that impacts millions of animals and their caregivers. We operate in a fully remote environment, giving you the flexibility to do your best work while staying deeply connected to a fast-moving, highly collaborative team.\n\n \n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n \n\n - Lead the architecture, design, and delivery of large scale frontend applications across web and mobile\n\n - Build and evolve high performance React and React Native applications\n\n - Define and enforce frontend best practices, including performance optimization, accessibility, and maintainability\n\n - Develop shared component libraries, design systems, and frontend infrastructure to improve team velocity\n\n - Drive improvements in application performance, reliability, and user experience\n\n - Partner closely with product managers, designers, and backend engineers to deliver cohesive, user centered features\n\n - Mentor junior front end engineers\n\n - Influence technical direction and frontend strategy across multiple product areas\n\n - Debug and resolve complex frontend and cross stack issues\n\n \n\nWhat We’re Looking For\n\n \n\n - 8+ years of software engineering experience, with a strong focus on frontend development\n\n - Experience building Claude/Cursor skills to help streamline FE best practices\n\n - Bachelor’s degree required, CS or technical degree preferred\n\n - Deep expertise in JavaScript/TypeScript and modern frontend frameworks (especially React)\n\n - Experience architecting and scaling complex frontend applications and systems\n\n - Strong understanding of performance optimization, state management, and frontend architecture patterns\n\n - Experience building and maintaining design systems or shared component libraries\n\n - Familiarity with mobile development (React Native or similar) is a plus\n\n - Solid understanding of APIs and backend interactions (REST, GraphQL, etc.)\n\n - Proven ability to lead projects and mentor engineers\n\n - Strong communication skills and a product-oriented mindset\n\n - Comfortable operating in fast paced, evolving environments\n\n \n\nTools We Use\n\n \n\n - Backend: Python (Django, Django Rest Framework)\n\n - Frontend: JavaScript (React, React-Query), TypeScript\n\n - Datastores: Postgres, Elasticsearch, Redis, Clickhouse\n\n - Mobile: React Native\n\n - Version Control: Git\n\n \n\nBenefits (Full Time Roles)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $170,000/year - $230,000/year + significant bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $190,000 - $220,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\nDetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted on an on going basis.\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a8955b40-7684-463d-b5f6-1a7ecf057bc2","title":"Head of Finance","department":"Finance","team":"Finance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T15:13:00.274+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/a8955b40-7684-463d-b5f6-1a7ecf057bc2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/a8955b40-7684-463d-b5f6-1a7ecf057bc2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is seeking a highly motivated and analytical <strong>Head of Finance (VP-Level)</strong> to lead our financial planning, strategy, and operations as we scale. Reporting directly to the Chief Executive Officer, this individual will oversee all aspects of accounting, FP&amp;A, budgeting, and financial reporting while serving as a key business partner to senior leadership across departments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate will bring both strategic and hands-on experience—someone who can build financial models, guide data-driven decision-making, and implement systems and controls to support rapid growth. You’ll play a critical role in ensuring financial transparency, driving operational efficiency, and positioning Vetcove for long-term success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You’ll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own financial strategy and planning</strong> — lead the company’s forecasting, budgeting, and long-range planning processes to ensure alignment with company goals and growth targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build an FP&amp;A function</strong> — develop scalable models, dashboards, and reporting to guide business decisions across revenue, margin, and expense performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Provide strategic business partnership</strong> — collaborate closely with department heads (e.g., Sales, Product, Operations, Customer Success) to translate financial insights into actionable strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Oversee accounting operations</strong> — manage general ledger, payroll, tax, invoicing, and reconciliations while ensuring compliance with GAAP and internal controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Develop and refine financial systems</strong> — identify and implement tools and processes to improve accuracy, efficiency, and visibility (e.g., ERP, expense management, analytics tools)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deliver timely and accurate reporting</strong> — prepare and present monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements, analyses, and board materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own cash flow management</strong> — forecast, track, and optimize cash receipts and disbursements to support business growth and operational needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead audits and tax filings</strong> — ensure compliance with all applicable accounting and tax regulations; serve as primary liaison with external auditors and advisors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive data-informed decision-making</strong> — analyze key metrics, unit economics, and business performance to inform pricing, investments, and resource allocation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and mentor the finance team</strong> — hire, develop, and lead a high-performing team capable of supporting a scaling, data-driven organization</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>You Should Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors Degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of experience in strategic finance ideally within a <strong>growth-stage or late-stage startup</strong> (eCommerce, SaaS, or marketplace experience preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in <strong>FP&amp;A, strategic finance, and operational modeling</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient knowledge of <strong>US GAAP</strong> and experience familiarity with executing  audits and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to design and implement <strong>financial planning processes and internal controls</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering cross-functionally with business leaders to drive performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced proficiency with <strong>QuickBooks (QBO preferred)</strong>, googlesheets / excel, finance software stack; Deep experience and desire to implement AI native solutions to drive efficiency, speed &amp; accuracyExcellent analytical and executive levelwritten, and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Benefits (Full-Time Roles)</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At-home office setup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $190,000/year - $250,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $200,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted November 1, 2026. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nVetcove is seeking a highly motivated and analytical Head of Finance (VP-Level) to lead our financial planning, strategy, and operations as we scale. Reporting directly to the Chief Executive Officer, this individual will oversee all aspects of accounting, FP&A, budgeting, and financial reporting while serving as a key business partner to senior leadership across departments.\n\n\n\nThe ideal candidate will bring both strategic and hands-on experience—someone who can build financial models, guide data-driven decision-making, and implement systems and controls to support rapid growth. You’ll play a critical role in ensuring financial transparency, driving operational efficiency, and positioning Vetcove for long-term success.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Own financial strategy and planning — lead the company’s forecasting, budgeting, and long-range planning processes to ensure alignment with company goals and growth targets\n\n - Build an FP&A function — develop scalable models, dashboards, and reporting to guide business decisions across revenue, margin, and expense performance\n\n - Provide strategic business partnership — collaborate closely with department heads (e.g., Sales, Product, Operations, Customer Success) to translate financial insights into actionable strategies\n\n - Oversee accounting operations — manage general ledger, payroll, tax, invoicing, and reconciliations while ensuring compliance with GAAP and internal controls\n\n - Develop and refine financial systems — identify and implement tools and processes to improve accuracy, efficiency, and visibility (e.g., ERP, expense management, analytics tools)\n\n - Deliver timely and accurate reporting — prepare and present monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements, analyses, and board materials\n\n - Own cash flow management — forecast, track, and optimize cash receipts and disbursements to support business growth and operational needs\n\n - Lead audits and tax filings — ensure compliance with all applicable accounting and tax regulations; serve as primary liaison with external auditors and advisors\n\n - Drive data-informed decision-making — analyze key metrics, unit economics, and business performance to inform pricing, investments, and resource allocation\n\n - Build and mentor the finance team — hire, develop, and lead a high-performing team capable of supporting a scaling, data-driven organization\n\n\n\n\nYOU SHOULD HAVE\n\n - Bachelors Degree\n\n - 8+ years of experience in strategic finance ideally within a growth-stage or late-stage startup (eCommerce, SaaS, or marketplace experience preferred)\n\n - Strong background in FP&A, strategic finance, and operational modeling\n\n - Proficient knowledge of US GAAP and experience familiarity with executing  audits and compliance\n\n - Proven ability to design and implement financial planning processes and internal controls\n\n - Experience partnering cross-functionally with business leaders to drive performance\n\n - Advanced proficiency with QuickBooks (QBO preferred), googlesheets / excel, finance software stack; Deep experience and desire to implement AI native solutions to drive efficiency, speed & accuracyExcellent analytical and executive levelwritten, and communication skills\n\n - Highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL-TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At-home office setup\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $190,000/year - $250,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $200,000 - $230,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more details.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is accepted November 1, 2026. \n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"466f325f-0b0b-4839-b4a9-eed94c114fa6","title":"Senior Manager, Strategic Events & Experiences","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T14:49:08.613+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Remote","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/466f325f-0b0b-4839-b4a9-eed94c114fa6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/vetcove/466f325f-0b0b-4839-b4a9-eed94c114fa6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone exceptional to own Vetcove’s most important in-person experiences, from multi-day leadership summits with our top customers and industry leaders to our annual company retreat and team offsites. You’ll take events from a broad idea to an exceptional experience, owning everything from the venue and programming to the budget, logistics, hospitality, and hundreds of details in between. This is a highly autonomous role for someone with exceptional taste, operational rigor, and hospitality instincts. We’ll give you the objective, not the playbook, and trust you to figure out how to create an experience people will remember.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own Vetcove’s major events end to end, from the first idea and event strategy through planning, execution, and the final guest departure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead our flagship customer and executive gatherings, annual company retreat, and team offsites, creating thoughtful, high-touch experiences for groups ranging from intimate executive gatherings to 200+ person events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn broad objectives into exceptionally detailed event plans spanning venues, programming, hospitality, travel, production, staffing, budgets, logistics, and the overall attendee experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Find exceptional hotels, venues, restaurants, speakers, and partners, build strong relationships with them, and negotiate aggressively and creatively to get the best possible experience and value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the clear owner across internal teams and external partners, driving decisions, timelines, budgets, and execution without requiring significant oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate what could go wrong before it does, from major logistical challenges to tiny details an attendee might notice, and solve the inevitable surprises quickly and calmly.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What we’re looking for</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience owning complex, high-touch events from start to finish, whether corporate events, executive gatherings, customer conferences, retreats, weddings, or similarly ambitious live experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You obsess over every detail. You notice the things others miss, think through the experience from every attendee’s perspective, and believe the smallest touches can be the difference between a good event and an exceptional one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve independently led complex, multi-day events and are comfortable keeping hundreds of decisions, dependencies, vendors, and logistics moving at once.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You genuinely love sourcing and negotiating. You enjoy finding the perfect hotel, venue, restaurant, or partner just as much as negotiating the contract, pushing for better terms, and figuring out how to make the budget go further.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have exceptional hospitality instincts and a strong sense of taste. You know how to make people feel genuinely welcomed and cared for, and you understand that something memorable doesn’t have to mean something extravagant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re remarkably resourceful and calm under pressure. When plans change or something goes wrong five minutes before guests arrive, your instinct is to take ownership, make a decision, and solve it.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Benefits (Full Time Roles)</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote within the USA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automatic 401k contribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employee referral program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At home office set up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bi-annual company retreats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open vacation policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly team events</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $100,000/year - $170,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. <strong>There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. </strong>For Colorado, the salary range is: $110,000 - $140,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />In addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits<br />package. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more<br />details.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">To apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Attention all job seekers!</strong> We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remember that during the application process, we will <em><strong>never</strong></em> request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Join Vetcove and help modernize the future of veterinary software and the pet parent healthcare experience. Our suite of platforms features a market-leading procurement marketplace, an ultra-modern home delivery ecommerce experience, and a next-generation practice management system. More than 25,000 hospitals across all 50 states rely on Vetcove daily, supporting tens of thousands of veterinarians who care for tens of millions of pets each year.\n\n\n\nWe are modernizing the 50 billion dollar plus animal health industry by giving veterinary organizations the tools to focus more on patient care. Backed by Y Combinator and top venture investors in Silicon Valley, New York and Miami, Vetcove is a fast-growing, mission-driven company. We are searching for talented and passionate people who want to help shape the future of veterinary care.\n\n\n\nWe’re looking for someone exceptional to own Vetcove’s most important in-person experiences, from multi-day leadership summits with our top customers and industry leaders to our annual company retreat and team offsites. You’ll take events from a broad idea to an exceptional experience, owning everything from the venue and programming to the budget, logistics, hospitality, and hundreds of details in between. This is a highly autonomous role for someone with exceptional taste, operational rigor, and hospitality instincts. We’ll give you the objective, not the playbook, and trust you to figure out how to create an experience people will remember.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own Vetcove’s major events end to end, from the first idea and event strategy through planning, execution, and the final guest departure.\n\n - Lead our flagship customer and executive gatherings, annual company retreat, and team offsites, creating thoughtful, high-touch experiences for groups ranging from intimate executive gatherings to 200+ person events.\n\n - Turn broad objectives into exceptionally detailed event plans spanning venues, programming, hospitality, travel, production, staffing, budgets, logistics, and the overall attendee experience.\n\n - Find exceptional hotels, venues, restaurants, speakers, and partners, build strong relationships with them, and negotiate aggressively and creatively to get the best possible experience and value.\n\n - Serve as the clear owner across internal teams and external partners, driving decisions, timelines, budgets, and execution without requiring significant oversight.\n\n - Anticipate what could go wrong before it does, from major logistical challenges to tiny details an attendee might notice, and solve the inevitable surprises quickly and calmly.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 7+ years of experience owning complex, high-touch events from start to finish, whether corporate events, executive gatherings, customer conferences, retreats, weddings, or similarly ambitious live experiences.\n\n - You obsess over every detail. You notice the things others miss, think through the experience from every attendee’s perspective, and believe the smallest touches can be the difference between a good event and an exceptional one.\n\n - You’ve independently led complex, multi-day events and are comfortable keeping hundreds of decisions, dependencies, vendors, and logistics moving at once.\n\n - You genuinely love sourcing and negotiating. You enjoy finding the perfect hotel, venue, restaurant, or partner just as much as negotiating the contract, pushing for better terms, and figuring out how to make the budget go further.\n\n - You have exceptional hospitality instincts and a strong sense of taste. You know how to make people feel genuinely welcomed and cared for, and you understand that something memorable doesn’t have to mean something extravagant.\n\n - You’re remarkably resourceful and calm under pressure. When plans change or something goes wrong five minutes before guests arrive, your instinct is to take ownership, make a decision, and solve it.\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS (FULL TIME ROLES)\n\n - 100% remote within the USA\n\n - Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n - Automatic 401k contribution\n\n - Employee referral program\n\n - At home office set up\n\n - Bi-annual company retreats\n\n - Open vacation policy\n\n - Equity\n\n - Monthly team events\n\n \n\nThe typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is: $100,000/year - $170,000/year + bonus + equity + benefits. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations. For Colorado, the salary range is: $110,000 - $140,000 + bonus + equity + benefits. This salary range is a good faith estimate of what Vetcove may pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on skills, qualifications, and experience. The range reflects the base hourly rate or annual compensation (as applicable), and does not include bonus, equity or other incentives.\n\n\nIn addition to base compensation, Vetcove offers a comprehensive benefits\npackage. Please refer to the “Benefits (Full Time Roles)” section above for more\ndetails.\n\n \n\nTo apply, please submit your application through Vetcove’s Careers Page. The application deadline is November 1st, 2026.\n\n\n\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor work visas at this time. \n\n\n\nAttention all job seekers! We want to ensure that you’re well-informed about a serious matter affecting the job market. It has come to our attention that scammers are operating in the industry, impersonating employees and attempting to deceive savvy applicants like you. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n 1. Our job listings are exclusively available on official sites (our careers page, LinkedIn, BuiltIn, and Indeed). Be cautious of other sources claiming to represent us or any organization that you’re interested in. Stay on the lookout!\n\n 2. Authentic communications from our company will only come through verified email addresses and phone numbers. If you receive unexpected messages or calls, exercise caution and verify their authenticity. Don’t let scammers catch you off guard!\n\n 3. It's essential to independently verify the legitimacy of any job postings you come across. Visit our official careers page to confirm the validity of any openings. Stay proactive and protect yourself!\n\n 4. Remember that during the application process, we will never request sensitive personal or financial information from you. Be wary of anyone asking for such information. Keep your personal data secure!\n\n 5. If you suspect any fraudulent activity or encounter suspicious individuals, please report it immediately to our recruiting department. By working together, we can combat these scams and keep the job market safer for everyone.\n\nWe understand the importance of your job search and want to ensure your experience is positive and secure. Always exercise caution and stay scam-smart!\n\n\n\nEmployment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\n\n\n\nVetcove is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other protected status. We are dedicated to providing a work environment free from discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all applicants in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. If you require accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know and we will make every effort to accommodate your needs.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}